\h Markos
\toc1 Markos
\toc2 Markos
\toc3 Mrk
\mt2 The account of Yeshua’s ministry by
\mt1 Markos
\is1 Introduction
\is2 Author
\ip This account about Yeshua’s activities and teachings was written by Markos (typically shortened to ‘Mark’ in English), the son of a Jewish family who lived in Yerushalem/Jerusalem. His mother was named Miryam/Mary (Acts 12:12).
\ip Many people think he was Yohan/John Markos, a cousin of Barnabas (Col. 4:10) who accompanied Paulos on his first long-distance trip to spread the good message about Yeshua the messiah (Acts 12:25, 13:13). We also know that Markos accompanied Kefa (1 Peter 5:13), and some consider that it might have been Kefa who narrated to Markos what Yeshua had done and taught.
\is2 This account
\ip This account seems to have been written for non-Jews, especially perhaps those familiar with Romaios customs. So he didn’t use as much ink as Matay or Lukas explaining prophecies from the Jewish scriptures but he does however, take time to explain Jewish customs to help non-Jewish readers.
\ip Markos explains here that Yeshua came to serve both God and the people, and he often refers to him as ‘the son of humanity’ (traditionally translated very literally from the Greek as the ‘Son of Man’). We can see that especially in 10:45: “Even the son of humanity didn’t come to be served, but to serve others and to give his life as a ransom to set many people free.” Markos wants his readers to know that Yeshua did incredible things, but especially focuses on Yeshua’s teaching. Markos confirms Yeshua’s power and authority by telling about the miracles that he did, his healing of the sick, and his exorcism of demons.
\ip The ending of this account is often disputed, and scholars are still \jmp debating|link-href="https://textandcanon.org/a-case-for-the-longer-ending-of-mark"\jmp* about whether or not the longer ending (16:9-20) is original to Markos. The \em OET\em* includes the disputed longer ending, but displays it in a lighter colour to indicate its debatable status.
\iot Main components of Markos’ account
\io1 Preparation for and arrival of the messiah \ior 1:1-13\ior*
\io1 Yeshua’s activities in and around Galil \ior 1:14–9:50\ior*
\io1 The transition from Galil to Yerushalem \ior 10:1-52\ior*
\io1 The final week in Yerushalem \ior 11:1–15:47\ior*
\io1 Yeshua comes back to life \ior 16:1-20\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\rem NOTE: This USFM file was exported from the ESFM source file with some loss of features, so don’t edit this derived file.
\c 1
\m
\v 1 \add Here\add* begins the good message \add about\add*\f + \fr 1:1 \ft As well as ‘about’, the Greek construction can also have the connotation of ‘brought by’, or even imply both. (\xt Yohan 1:1 \ft also confirms that Yeshua was both the messenger and the message itself.)\f* \nd God’s\nd* son, \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add the\add* \nd messiah\nd*:
\s1 The ministry of Yohan the immerser (The return of ‘Eliyah’)
\r (Mat. 3:1-12; Luke 3:1-18; Yhn. 1:19-28)
\p
\v 2 The prophet Yeshayah \add (Isaiah)\add* wrote:
\q1 “Look, I’m sending my messenger \add ahead of\add* you,
\q1 \add the one\add* who’ll be preparing your path.\x + \xo 1:2: \xt Mal 3:1.\x*
\q1
\v 3 The voice \add out\add* in the wilderness shouting,
\q2 ‘Get the path ready for \nd Yahweh\nd*—
\q2 make it smooth for him \add to walk on\add*.’ ”\x + \xo 1:3: \xt Isa 40:3 (LXX).\x*
\p
\v 4 Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* \add turned up\add* in the wilderness announcing that people should get \add immersed\add* \add in water\add* \add in order to show that\add* \add their\add* sins \add have been forgiven\add*,
\v 5 and \add many\add* from the Yehudah \add (Judea)\add* region and from Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* \add city\add* went out to \add hear\add* him, and \add asked Yohan\add* to immerse them in the Yarden \add (Jordan)\add* river as they confessed their sins.
\p
\v 6 Yohan was dressed in \add simple clothes made from\add* camel \add hair\add* with a leather belt around his waist,\x + \xo 1:6: \xt 2Ki 1:8.\x* and he \add lived on\add* locusts and wild honey.
\v 7 He \add also\add* announced, “There’s a greater \add man\add* coming \add soon\add*—\add in fact\add* I’m not \add even good enough\add* to bend down and untie his sandal \add straps\add*.
\v 8 I immersed you all in water, but he’ll immerse you in \add God’s\add* holy \nd spirit\nd*.”
\s1 Yeshua gets immersed and then tempted
\r (Mat. 3:13–4:11; Luke 3:21-22; 4:1-13)
\p
\v 9 \fig Yeshua was immersed by Yohan.|src="images/41_Mk_01_06_RG.jpg" size="col" loc="1:9" copy="© Sweet Publishing" ref="1:9"\fig*\add Then one day\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* came from Nazaret \add (Nazareth)\add* in the Galil \add region\add*, and he got immersed in the Yarden \add (Jordan)\add* \add river\add* by Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add*.
\v 10 \add As\add* \add Yeshua\add* came up out of the water, he saw the sky being \add opened up\add*, and \add God’s\add* \nd spirit\nd* coming down on him like a dove.
\v 11 And a voice came from the sky \add saying\add*, “You’re my son who I love \add and\add* \add am pleased with\add*.”\x + \xo 1:11: \xt Gen 22:2; Psa 2:7; Isa 42:1; Mat 3:17; 12:18; Mrk 9:7; Luk 3:22.\x*
\p
\v 12 \add After that,\add* the \nd spirit\nd* sent him \add out\add* into the wilderness
\v 13 \add where\add* he was tested by Satan for forty days. He was \add out there\add* with the wild animals, but \add God’s\add* messengers\f + \fr 1:13 \ft The Greek doesn’t actually distinguish between human messengers and heavenly messengers (so-called ‘angels’—the Greek word just transliterated letter-by-letter instead of being actually translated).\f* \add looked after\add* him \add there\add*.
\s1 The selection of the first followers/apprentices
\r (Mat. 4:12-22; Luke 4:14-15; 5:1-11)
\p
\v 14 After Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* had been \add arrested\add*, \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* went back up \add north\add* to Galil, announcing the good news from \nd God\nd*
\v 15 saying, “\wj The \+add promised time is here\+add*, and \nd God’s\nd* kingdom is \+add now\+add* near. \+add Turn from your sins\+add* and believe this good news.\wj*”\x + \xo 1:15: \xt Mat 3:2.\x*
\p
\v 16 As he went around Lake Galil, \add Yeshua\add* saw \add two\add* fishermen, Shim’on \add (Simon)\add* and \add his\add* brother Andreas, throwing a net into the lake
\v 17 and \add he\add* said to them, “\wj Come \+add with\+add* me and I’ll make you into fishers of people.\wj*”
\v 18 \add So\add* they left their \add fishing work\add* and \add went off with\add* \add Yeshua\add*.
\p
\v 19 Then a bit further on he saw \add two\add* of Zavday’s \add (Grk. Zebedaios)\add* sons, Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and his brother Yohan, in a boat getting the nets ready.
\v 20 \add Yeshua\add* called them and they \add too\add* \add went off with\add* him, leaving their father Zavday in the boat with the hired workers.
\s1 Yeshua drives out a demon
\r (Luke 4:31-37)
\p
\v 21 They \add went on\add* into Kafarnaoum \add (Capernaum)\add* \add where\add* as soon as a rest \add day\add* started, he would go into the \add Jewish meeting hall\add* \add (Grk. synagogue)\add* \add and\add* teach \add there\add*.
\v 22 \add The congregation\add* was amazed at his teaching, because he taught like \add someone\add* with authority, not like the \add regular teachers\add* \add there\add*.\x + \xo 1:22: \xt Mat 7:28-29.\x*
\p
\v 23 Then a \add demon-possessed\add* man in the \add meeting hall\add* suddenly yelled out,
\v 24 “What are we to you, \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* of Nazaret \add (Nazareth)\add*? You’ve come to destroy us. I know that you’re \nd God’s\nd* holy \add one\add*.”
\p
\v 25 But \nd Yeshua\nd* scolded \add it\add*,\f + \fr 1:25 \ft The Greek pronoun is masculine, implying that the man was the one being scolded, yet “Come out of him!” implies that the spirit is being spoken to.\f* saying, “\wj Keep quiet!\wj*”, and, “\wj Come out of him!\wj*”
\p
\v 26 Then the demon \add threw the man into a convulsion\add*, cried out \add loudly\add*, and \add left\add* him.
\v 27 Everyone was astounded \add and asked each other\add*, “What \add just happened\add*? \add We\add* \add haven’t heard anything like this before\add*\add —he has authority to command demons, and they obey\add* him!”
\v 28 \add So then\add* the news about \add Yeshua\add* spread all over \add that entire\add* Galil region.
\s1 Yeshua heals many others
\r (Mat. 8:14-17; Luke 4:38-41)
\p
\v 29 After leaving the \add meeting hall\add*, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* went with Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* into the home of Shim’on \add (Simon)\add* and Andreas.
\v 30 \add Inside,\add* Shim’on’s mother-in-law was lying down \add with a fever\add*, and \add the others\add* spoke to \add Yeshua\add* about her.
\v 31 When \add he went up to her, and\add* took hold of her hand \add and\add* \add helped her up\add*, the fever left her and she \add prepared something for them to eat\add*.
\p
\v 32 \add That\add* evening when the sun set, \add the people\add* brought all those \add who were sick or\add* demon-possessed to \add Yeshua\add*.
\v 33 \add It seemed like\add* the \add entire\add* town had gathered there \add outside\add* the \add front\add* door.
\v 34 \add Yeshua\add* healed many \add who were sick from a range of\add* diseases, and he \add commanded many demons to leave\add*—not allowing \add them\add* to speak because they knew that he was \nd the messiah\nd*.
\s1 Yeshua prays before going preaching
\r (Luke 4:42-44)
\p
\v 35 In the \add small hours of\add* the morning, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add got up\add* and went out to a quiet place and prayed there.
\v 36 \add But\add* Shim’on \add (Simon)\add* and the others \add came\add* looking for him,
\v 37 and \add when\add* they found him they said, “Everyone’s \add looking for\add* you!”
\p
\v 38 “\wj \+add Well,\+add*\wj*” \add Yeshua\add* answered, “\wj we’ll be going into the \+add other villages around here\+add*, so that I can also tell \+add them\+add*. \+add That’s what I came here for\+add*.\wj*”
\v 39 Then he went preaching in all their \add meeting halls\add* in Galil, and \add driving\add* out demons.\x + \xo 1:39: \xt Mat 4:23; 9:35.\x*
\s1 Yeshua heals a man with leprosy
\r (Mat. 8:1-4; Luke 5:12-16)
\p
\v 40 \add One day,\add* a \add man with leprosy\add* came to \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* asking him, “\add I know that you could heal me if you wanted to\add*.”
\p
\v 41 \add Yeshua\add* felt compassion \add for him\add*, \add reached\add* out his hand and touched \add him\add*, and said, “\wj \+add Yes, I will. Get well\+add*.\wj*”
\v 42 Then immediately the leprosy \add disappeared\add* and he was \add well again\add*.
\v 43 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* sent him \add away\add*, \add but\add* warned him:
\v 44 “\wj Don’t talk to anyone—\+add just\+add* go to the priest and show him \+add that you’re well\+add*, and as a testimony of that, make the offering that Mosheh \+add (Moses)\+add* commanded \+add so as to be declared clean again\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 1:44: \xt Lev 14:1-32.\x*
\p
\v 45 But \add after the man left\add*, he started telling \add lots of people\add* and spreading the news—\add so much\add* so that \add Yeshua\add* could no longer come into the town but had to stay out in \add quieter\add* places, and \add people\add* \add kept\add* coming to him.
\c 2
\s1 Yeshua heals a paralysed man
\r (Mat. 9:1-8; Luke 5:17-26)
\p
\v 1 \add When\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* went \add back\add* to Kafarnaoum \add (Capernaum)\add* \add after a few\add* days, \add people soon\add* heard that he was \add back\add* in the house
\v 2 and \add so\add* many people \add turned up there\add* that there wasn’t any room left—not even in the doorway. \add Inside,\add* \add Yeshua\add* was \add explaining the scriptures\add* to them.
\v 3 Four \add men arrived, carrying a paralysed man\add* to \add Yeshua\add*,
\v 4 \add but\add* because of the crowd, \add they were unable to get close\add*. \add So\add* they \add climbed up onto the flat\add* roof, \add removed a section\add*, and lowered the \add paralysed man\add* lying on a pallet.
\v 5 \nd Yeshua\nd*, observing their faith, said to the \add man\add*, “\wj Son, your sins are forgiven!\wj*”\f + \fr 2:5 \ft Yeshua’s hearers would have taken this as a claim to be God, as they knew that only God could forgive sins as v7 shows.\f*
\p
\v 6 But some of the \add religious teachers\add* were sitting there, \add thinking to themselves\add*,
\v 7 “Why’s that fellow talking like that? He’s \add seriously insulting\add* God. \add There’s only\add* one who can forgive sins, \add and that’s\add* \nd God\nd* \add himself\add*.”
\p
\v 8 Then \nd Yeshua\nd*, knowing in his spirit that they were reasoning like that, said to them, “\wj Why are you \+add thinking that to yourselves\+add*?\wj*
\v 9 \wj Which is easier: to tell the \+add paralysed man\+add* that his sins have been forgiven, or to tell him to pick up his \+add bedding\+add* and walk?\wj*
\v 10 \wj But so you all can see that the son of humanity \+em does\+em* have authority here on the earth to forgive sins,\wj*” he \add turned and\add* said to the \add paralysed man\add*,
\v 11 “\wj \+add Listen\+add*. Get up, take your \+add bedding\+add*, and go home!\wj*”
\p
\v 12 \add So\add* \add the man\add* stood up, and picked up \add his bedding\add*, and went \add outside, where everyone saw him\add* and marvelled and \add praised\add* \nd God\nd* saying, “We’ve never seen \add anything like that\add* \add happen before\add*!”
\s1 Levi’s (Matthew’s) calling
\r (Mat. 9:9-13; Luke 5:27-32)
\p
\v 13 \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* went \add back\add* out beside the lake where \add crowds of people\add* kept coming to him and he taught them.
\v 14 As he was passing by the tax office, he saw Levi Halfay \add (Grk. Halfaios)\add* sitting \add there\add* and said to him, “\add Come along with\add* me.” \add So\add* \add Levi\add* stood up and followed \add Yeshua\add*.
\p
\v 15 \add Yeshua\add* \add ended up having a meal\add* at \add Levi’s\add* \add place\add*, and many \add other\add* tax collectors and \add undesirables\add* were sitting \add there also\add*, along \nd with Yeshua\nd* and his followers, because \add by then\add*, many \add people\add* were following him \add around\add*.
\v 16 \add When\add* the teachers from the Farisaios party \add noticed\add* that \add Yeshua\add* was eating \add beside undesirables\add* and tax-collectors, they \add asked\add* his followers, “\add How come\add* he eats with tax-collectors and \add other low-life\add*?”
\p
\v 17 \nd Yeshua\nd* \add overheard\add* them and said, “\wj Healthy people don’t need a doctor—it’s the sick ones that do. I didn’t come \+add here\+add* to \+add help those who think they have no needs\+add*, but \+add I came\+add* to call sinners.\wj*”
\s1 The question of fasting
\r (Mat. 9:14-17; Luke 5:33-39)
\p
\v 18 \add Now\add* the followers of Yohan-the-immerser, and \add members of\add* the Farisaios party, \add regularly\add* fasted. \add So\add* \add a small group\add* came to \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and asked, “\add How come\add* Yohan’s \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* followers and the Farisaios party fast \add regularly\add*, yet your followers don’t?”
\p
\v 19 “\wj Can the \+add groomsmen\+add* fast when they’re \+add celebrating\+add* along with him?\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add answered\add*, “\wj \+add No,\+add* as long as \+add he’s\+add* still there, they \+add won’t be\+add* fasting.\wj*
\v 20 \wj But \+add in the future\+add*, the groom will be taken away from them, and \+em then\+em* they’ll be fasting.\wj*
\p
\v 21 “\wj No one sews a patch of \+add new\+add*, unshrunken cloth onto \+add used clothes\+add*, because the \+add new\+add* patch will tear away from that old fabric, and it will \+add end up with\+add* a worse tear.\wj*
\v 22 \wj And no one puts new wine into old wineskin \+add containers\+add*, because the wine will burst the \+add already stretched\+add* wineskins, and then both the wine and the wineskins will be destroyed. New wine must be put into \+em new\+em* wineskins.\wj*”
\s1 Working on the Rest Day
\r (Mat. 12:1-8; Luke 6:1-5)
\p
\v 23 \add Then it so happened that\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and his followers passed through some fields of grain on some days of rest. \add As they went through\add*, they plucked off some heads of grain,\x + \xo 2:23: \xt Deu 23:25.\x*
\v 24 and \add some members of\add* the Farisaios party said, “\add Hey, it’s breaking the law to harvest grain\add* on a rest \add day\add*!”
\p
\v 25 “\wj You’ve read \+add yourselves\+add*,\wj*” \add Yeshua\add* \add replied\add*, “\wj what David did when he and his men were hungry.\wj*
\v 26 \wj \+add They\+add* went into \+nd God’s\+nd* \+add tent\+add* and ate the \+add sacred\+add* bread \+add representing\+add* \+add God’s\+add* presence. Only the priests \+add were allowed to eat that\+add*,\x + \xo 2:26: \xt Lev 24:9.\x* and yet \+add David\+add* even gave some to his \+add companions\+add*!\wj*”
\v 27 Then he told the \add Farisaios\add*, “\wj The \+add days\+add* of rest \+add were created for people\+add*, not \+add people\+add* for the rest \+add days\+add*.\wj*
\v 28 \wj So \+add I\+add*, the son of humanity, \+add have authority also over\+add* the day of rest.\wj*”
\c 3
\s1 The man with the curled-up hand
\r (Mat. 12:9-14; Luke 6:6-11)
\p
\v 1 Again \add at another time\add*, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* went into the \add Jewish meeting hall\add* and there was a man there with a curled-up hand.
\v 2 The \add religious leaders there\add* were watching him closely \add to see\add* if he would heal the man on the rest \add day\add*, \add and then if he did, they would have a case\add* against him.
\v 3 Then \add Yeshua\add* said to the man with the flawed hand, “\wj \+add Stand up there\+add* in the middle.\wj*”
\v 4 And he asked \add the leaders\add*, “\wj Is it allowable to do good on the rest \+add day\+add*, or \+add only\+add* to do evil? To save life, or to kill?\wj*” But they \add didn’t reply\add*.
\p
\v 5 After \add angrily\add* looking around at them, grieving at \add their complete lack of compassion\add*, he told the man, “\wj \+add Open up\+add* your hand!\wj*” The man stretched out \add his fingers\add*, and his hand \add became totally normal\add*.
\v 6 \add But\add* the Farisaios \add quickly left\add*, and \add meeting\add* with \add King\add* Herodes’s \add (Herod)\add* supporters, they \add conspired to kill\add* \add Yeshua\add*.
\s1 Big crowds press against Yeshua
\p
\v 7 \add After that,\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* withdrew towards the lake with his apprentices \add as well as\add* a huge crowd \add of people\add* from the \add regions of both\add* Galil and \add down in\add* Yehudah \add (Judea)\add*,
\v 8 \add along with others\add* from Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add*, Idoumaia, from across the Yarden \add (Jordan)\add* \add River\add*, and from \add up\add* near Tsor \add (Tyre)\add* and Tsidon \add (Sidon)\add*. That huge crowd came \add because\add* they had heard about the \add amazing\add* things he had done.
\v 9 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* asked his apprentices \add to organise\add* a small boat to be there for him so he wouldn’t be cramped by \add the press of\add* the crowd.\x + \xo 3:9-10: \xt Mrk 4:1; Luk 5:1-3.\x*
\v 10 \add Virtually anyone who had any physical issues\add* was pressing towards him to touch him, because he had \add already\add* healed so many.
\v 11 And the \add demons\add*, whenever they \add saw\add* \add Yeshua\add*, they fell \add to their knees on\add* the ground \add in front of\add* him and yelled out, “You are \nd God’s\nd* son!”
\v 12 \add However\add* he \add regularly\add* warned them not to \add reveal who he was\add*.
\s1 Yeshua appoints his twelve representatives
\r (Mat. 10:1-4; Luke 6:12-16)
\p
\v 13 As \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add started\add* going up a hill, he called the followers \add that he had selected\add* and they went off with him.
\v 14 He appointed twelve \add of them\add* as his representatives so that they could \add stick\add* with him, and be sent off to be proclaiming \add his message\add*
\v 15 and to also have authority to exorcise demons.
\p
\v 16 \add These are\add* the twelve that he appointed: Shim’on \add (Simon)\add* (but he appended the name “Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add*”),
\v 17 Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and \add his\add* brother Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* who were Zavday’s \add (Grk. Zebedaios)\add* sons (and he nicknamed them the “sons of thunder”),
\v 18 Andreas, Filippos \add (Philip)\add*, Bar-Talmay \add (Bartholomew; Grk. Bartholomaios)\add*, Matay \add (Matthew; Grk. Matthaios)\add*, Toma \add (Thomas)\add*, Ya’akov Halfay \add (Grk. Halfaios)\add*, Thaddaios \add (Thaddeus)\add*, Shim’on \add from\add* Kena’an \add (Canaan)\add*,
\v 19 and Yehudah \add (Judas; Grk. Yudas)\add* Iskariot who \add later\add* betrayed him.
\s1 The two opposing spiritual powers
\r (Mat. 12:22-32; Luke 11:14-23; 12:10)
\p
\v 20 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* was approaching a house, but the crowd \add swarmed them\add* again so they \add had no opportunity\add* to eat.
\v 21 The ones with him heard \add all the noise\add* and came to get him, because they were \add wondering if he was crazy\add*.
\p
\v 22 The \add religious teachers\add* had come \add up\add* from Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* and were \add complaining\add*, “\add He’s possessed by the prince of demons\add*. He \add can command\add* \add them\add* because \add he rules\add* \add them\add*!”\x + \xo 3:22: \xt Mat 9:34; 10:25.\x*
\p
\v 23 \add But\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add addressed\add* them: “\wj How could Satan \+add command\+add* \+add himself\+add*?\wj*
\v 24 \wj If a kingdom is divided against itself, that kingdom \+add could never prosper\+add*.\wj*
\v 25 \wj If a \+add household\+add* is divided against itself, that \+add family will never prosper\+add*.\wj*
\v 26 \wj \+add So\+add* if Satan \+add attacked\+add* himself and was split, he \+add couldn’t possibly be powerful\+add*, but \+add his time would be over\+add*.\wj*
\p
\v 27 \wj \+add On the contrary\+add*, no one can enter a strong man’s house to \+add clean out his possessions\+add* unless he first ties up that strong man—\+add after that he can work on the goods\+add*.\wj*
\p
\v 28 \wj \+add Honestly, I assure\+add* you that any sins of a \+add person\+add* can be forgiven, \+add no matter how much they curse\+add* \+add God\+add*.\wj*
\v 29 \wj But anyone who \+add speaks against\+add* the Holy \+nd Spirit\+nd* can \+add never\+add* \+add be forgiven\+add*, but is eternally \+add responsible\+add* for \+add their\+add* sin.\wj*”\x + \xo 3:29: \xt Luk 12:10.\x*
\v 30 (\add He said that\add* because they were saying that he was \add demon-possessed\add*.)
\s1 Yeshua’s mother and brothers arrive
\r (Mat. 12:46-50; Luke 8:19-21)
\p
\v 31 \add Now\add* \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* mother and brothers came and were standing outside, and they \add asked someone to tell him that they were there\add*.
\v 32 \add Some in\add* the crowd sitting around him told \add Yeshua\add* that his mother and brothers were \add waiting outside for him\add*.
\p
\v 33 \add But\add* \add Yeshua\add* answered, “\wj Who is my mother and \+add who are\+add* my brothers?\wj*”
\v 34 And having looked around at the \add people\add* sitting here, he said, “\wj \+add Actually, you all are\+add* my mother and my brothers,\wj*
\v 35 \wj because anyone who \+add obeys\+add* \+nd God\+nd*, that \+add person\+add* is my brother and my sister and my mother.\wj*”
\c 4
\s1 The parable about planting seed
\r (Mat. 13:1-9; Luke 8:4-8)
\p
\v 1 Again \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* started teaching \add by the edge of\add* the lake. A huge crowd gathered \add around\add* him, \add but\add* he had boarded a boat that was \add floating in the water\add*, and all the people were \add there\add* on the \add shore\add*.\x + \xo 4:1: \xt Luk 5:1-3.\x*
\v 2 \add From there\add*, he taught them many \add different\add* things in parables, \add including this one\add*:
\v 3 “\wj Listen. \+add Once there was a farmer\+add* who went to \+add spread some seed\+add*.\wj*
\v 4 \wj \+add As he spread it\+add*, some landed on the path, and the birds came and \+add fed on\+add* it.\wj*
\v 5 \wj \+add Some\+add* landed on \+add a rocky part without a lot of\+add* soil, and it \+add quickly sprouted\+add* in the \+add warm\+add*, \+add shallow\+add* soil,\wj*
\v 6 \wj \+add but\+add* when the sun came up, it \+add dried out\+add* because \+add the roots weren’t deep\+add*, \+add and so\+add* it \+add just\+add* withered up.\wj*
\v 7 \wj \+add Some of the seed landed in a thistle patch\+add*, and the thistles \+add grew\+add* and choked it out, \+add so the plants never bore a crop\+add*.\wj*
\v 8 \wj \+add But some\+add* \+add seed\+add* landed in \+add fertile\+add* soil and it \+add bore a harvest\+add*—\+add some of\+add* it \+add multiplying\+add* thirty \+add times\+add*, some sixty, and some a hundred \+add times\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 9 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add added\add*, “\wj \+add Anyone who wants to understand\+add*, let them \+add consider it\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Why Yeshua speaks in parables
\r (Mat. 13:10-17; Luke 8:9-10)
\p
\v 10 \add Later\add* when \add the crowd had left\add*, the twelve \add apprentices\add* asked him about the parables
\v 11 and he told them, “\wj You’ve \+add been given understanding\+add* about \nd God’s\nd* kingdom, but \+add for others\+add*, \+add they’ll get it\+add* in parables\wj*
\q1
\v 12 \wj so that \+add when they look\+add*, they might see \+add but\+add* not perceive,\wj*
\q1 \wj and \+add when they listen\+add*, they might hear \+add but\+add* not understand,\wj*
\q1 \wj otherwise they might turn \+add from their sins\+add* and \+add be\+add* forgiven.\wj*”\x + \xo 4:12: \xt Isa 6:9-10 (LXX).\x*
\s1 The ground where the seed fell
\r (Mat. 13:18-23; Luke 8:11-15)
\p
\v 13 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* said to them, “\wj \+add If you didn’t understand\+add* this parable, how will you \+add understand any others\+add*?\wj*
\v 14 \wj The \+add person\+add* \+add spreading\+add* seed is \+add spreading\+add* the \+add good\+add* message,\wj*
\v 15 \wj and \+add there are some\+add* along the path where the \+add good\+add* message is being \+add spread\+add*, who hear, \+add but\+add* Satan \+add turns up\+add* immediately and \+add snatches\+add* the message that had been \+add planted\+add* in them.\wj*
\v 16 \wj Similarly, there’s \+add some seed\+add* that falls onto rocky places where \+add the people\+add* who hear the \+add good\+add* message \+add happily accept\+add* it,\wj*
\v 17 \wj \+add but\+add* don’t \+add make strong roots\+add*—\+add just\+add* temporary \+add changes\+add*. \+add So when they get mocked or attacked about accepting\+add* the \+add good\+add* message, they \+add quickly\+add* stumble.\wj*
\v 18 \wj Others are the ones \+add where the seed was spread\+add* among the thistles. They heard the \+add good message\+add*,\wj*
\v 19 \wj \+add but contemporary topics\+add*, \+add or the lure of money\+add*, or the appetite for other \+add things\+add*, choke \+add their good intentions\+add* and \+add the message\+add* becomes unfruitful \+add in them\+add*.\wj*
\v 20 \wj \+add But\+add* \+add lastly\+add*, \+add the seed\+add* that landed on the good soil \+add represents\+add* \+add the people\+add* who hear the \+add good\+add* message, accept it, and are \+add fruitful\+add* thirty, sixty, or \+add even\+add* a hundred times \+add over\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 The light will shine on everything
\r (Luke 8:16-18)
\p
\v 21 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* told them, “\wj \+add Obviously no one goes and gets a\+add* lamp, \+add and then\+add* puts it under a basket or under the bed, \+add but rather they place\+add* it \+add somewhere higher\+add* on a stand.\wj*\x + \xo 4:21: \xt Mat 5:15; Luk 11:33.\x*
\v 22 \wj \+add You see, nothing\+add* is hidden \+add that won’t\+add* \+add eventually\+add* be disclosed, and there’s no secret that won’t \+add eventually\+add* \+add be revealed\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 4:22: \xt Mat 10:26; Luk 12:2.\x*
\v 23 \wj Anyone who \+add wants to understand must listen carefully\+add*,\wj*”
\v 24 and he continued, “\wj \+add Take care what you listen to\+add*. \+add How much you all judge others, so too will judgement be handed out\+add* to you, and \+add even more\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 4:24: \xt Mat 7:2; Luk 6:38.\x* DOUBLE-CHECK
\v 25 \wj Anyone who has \+add faith\+add* will be given \+add a reward\+add*, \+add but if you have none\+add*, even \+add the little\+add* \+add you\+add* have will be taken away.\wj*”\x + \xo 4:25: \xt Mat 13:12; 25:29; Luk 19:26.\x* DOUBLE-CHECK
\s1 The parable about the sprouting seed
\p
\v 26 And then, “\wj \nd God’s\nd* kingdom is like a \+add person\+add* throwing \+add some\+add* seed onto the ground.\wj*
\v 27 \wj \+add Whether\+add* \+add the person\+add* sleeps \+add at night\+add* or \+add stays up\+add* night and day, the seed will sprout and grow \+add either way\+add*, and \+add they\+add* don’t know how \+add it does it\+add*.\wj*
\v 28 \wj The earth is \+add designed\+add* \+add to multiply the seed\+add*: first a \+add sprout\+add* \+add appears\+add*, then a \+add bigger plant\+add*, and then the full head of grain.\wj*
\v 29 \wj \+add Then when it’s ripe\+add*, \+add the harvester\+add* is sent in because \+add it’s ready for\+add* harvest.\wj*”\x + \xo 4:29: \xt Yoel 3:13.\x*
\s1 The small seed produces a large result
\r (Mat. 13:31-32,34; Luke 13:18-19)
\p
\v 30 \add Again\add* he said, “\wj What could we liken \nd God’s\nd* kingdom to? Or what parable could we \+add explain it with\+add*?\wj*
\v 31 \wj It’s like \+add planting\+add* a mustard seed in the ground—\+add a very small seed\+add*.\wj*
\v 32 \wj \+add But\+add* when it’s \+add planted and grows up\+add*, it \+add forms a large bush with many\+add* branches so that birds can nest in its \+add shade\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 33 And \add so as much as they could handle it\add*, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add shared\add* the \add good\add* message with them \add via many similar word pictures\add*.
\v 34 He \add never spoke without those illustrations\add*, but he explained all of them to his \add close\add* followers.
\s1 Yeshua halts the storm on the lake
\r (Mat. 8:23-27; Luke 8:22-25)
\p
\v 35 \add It was already\add* becoming evening on that day, \add so\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* told \add his apprentices\add*, “\wj Let’s \+add all\+add* \+add go across to the other shore\+add*.\wj*”
\v 36 Then after sending the crowd away, they got into the boat with him, plus there were \add some\add* other boats with \add them\add*.
\v 37 \add Out on the lake,\add* a big storm \add came up with strong winds\add*, and the waves started breaking \add across\add* the boat and filling it \add with water\add*.
\v 38 \add However,\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add was asleep\add* on a cushion in the back, \add so\add* they woke him, \add calling out\add*, “Teacher, don’t you care that we’re \add all about to drown\add*?”
\p
\v 39 \add Now awake\add*, \add Yeshua\add* scolded the wind and \add waves\add*, “\wj Quieten down! Stop that!\wj*” Then the wind died down and \add the lake\add* became very calm.
\v 40 \add Turning back to them\add* he \add asked\add*, “\wj Why were you all afraid? Don’t you have \+add any\+add* faith yet?\wj*”
\p
\v 41 \add But now\add* they were \add very\add* afraid \add again\add*, and \add asked\add* each other, “Who could this \add man\add* be that both the wind and the \add waves obey\add* him?”
\c 5
\s1 Yeshua sends the demons into pigs
\r (Mat. 8:28-34; Luke 8:26-39)
\p
\v 1 \add So\add* they got \add safely\add* to the Gerasainon region on the \add other\add* side of the lake.
\v 2 As \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add climbed\add* out of the boat, a \add demon-possessed\add* man \add came\add* out of the tombs to meet him.
\v 3 He \add lived\add* in \add those\add* tombs, and no one could tie him up, not even with \add chains\add*,
\v 4 because he had often been tied up \add in the past\add* with shackles and chains but had always pulled the chains apart and \add smashed\add* the shackles, and no one was able to subdue him.
\v 5 All through the day and night, \add whether\add* in the tombs or \add up\add* in the hills, he was yelling out and \add hurting\add* himself with stones.
\p
\v 6 \add So\add* when he had seen \nd Yeshua\nd* in the distance, he ran and \add as a sign of honour\add* fell to \add his knees on the ground\add* in front of him.
\v 7 Then he called out \add very loudly\add*, “What \add will happen between us\add*, \nd Yeshua\nd*—the son \nd of\nd* the highest \nd God\nd*? I beg you in \nd God’s\nd* \add name\add* not to torment me.”
\v 8 Because \add Yeshua\add* had \add already started\add* saying, “\wj Come out of the man you \+add ungodly\+add* spirit!\wj*”
\p
\v 9 \add Yeshua\add* asked, “\wj What’s your name?\wj*”
\p The man \add answered\add*, “My name is ‘Thousands’ because there’s many of us,”
\v 10 and he begged \add Yeshua\add* not to send them out of the country.
\p
\v 11 \add It just so happened that\add* there was a large herd of pigs being fed near the hill,
\v 12 and \add the demons\add* begged \add Yeshua\add* \add again\add* saying, “Send us to the pigs so that we can enter them.”
\v 13 \add Yeshua\add* \add agreed to that\add*, \add so\add* the \add ungodly\add* spirits came out \add of the man\add*, went into the pigs, and the \add entire\add* herd of some two thousand \add pigs\add* rushed down the steep bank into the lake and were drowned.
\p
\v 14 The ones who had been feeding them \add rushed off\add* and \add spread the news around\add* in the city and the \add surrounding area, So\add* \add the people\add* \add hurried\add* out to see what had happened.
\v 15 \add When they arrived where\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* was, they saw the man who had been demon-possessed, \add fully-\add*clothed and \add sitting there in full control of his senses\add*. \add They knew it was\add* the \add man\add* called ‘Thousands’ and they \add became frightened\add*.
\v 16 Those who had seen it all happen described it \add all\add* to \add the people\add*—\add what had happened\add* \add both\add* to the demon-possessed \add man\add* and to the pigs.
\p
\v 17 \add So\add* then the people \add began\add* asking \add Yeshua\add* to go away from their \add region\add*.
\p
\v 18 \add As\add* \add Yeshua\add* was \add climbing back\add* into the boat, the \add man\add* who had been demon-possessed \add wanted\add* to go with him.
\v 19 \add But\add* \add Yeshua\add* wouldn’t let him and told him \add to head back\add* home to his own people, and \add explain\add* to them what the \nd master\nd* had done for him, and \add how\add* he had been merciful to him.
\p
\v 20 \add So\add* he went away and \add shared with\add* \add the people in\add* the Ten Cities \add region\add* what \nd Yeshua\nd* had done for him, and they were all amazed.
\s1 A woman healed as Yeshua goes to help a dying girl
\r (Mat. 9:18-26; Luke 8:40-56)
\p
\v 21 \add When\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* had crossed in the boat \add to the other side\add* \add of the lake\add*, a large crowd \add of people\add* \add came out to the lake edge to see\add* him.
\v 22 Then \add unexpectedly\add*, one of the \add religious\add* leaders named Yair \add (Jairus)\add* came out, and \add when he found\add* \add Yeshua\add*, he fell \add to his knees in front of him\add*
\v 23 and pleaded, “My \add young\add* daughter is \add critical and\add* \add just hanging on\add* for you to come and \add touch\add* her so that she’ll be healed and live.”
\p
\v 24 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* went off with \add Yair\add*. The large crowd followed \add also\add*, and \add many were getting pressed against\add* \add Yeshua\add*.
\p
\v 25 Then a woman \add came who\add* \add had been losing\add* blood for twelve years,
\v 26 and who’d endured much under \add various\add* doctors \add despite spending everything she had\add*. \add After all that, she’d ended up even\add* worse,
\v 27 \add but\add* when she heard about what \nd Yeshua\nd* \add had been doing\add*, \add she worked her way through\add* the crowd \add to the back of\add* \add Yeshua and\add* touched his \add clothes\add*,
\v 28 because she had told \add herself\add*, “If I could even just touch his clothes, I’d be healed.”
\p
\v 29 Immediately the \add bleeding stopped\add*, and she knew that she had been healed.
\v 30 Immediately \add also\add*, \nd Yeshua\nd* knew that power had gone out of him, \add and\add* he turned back towards the crowd \add and\add* said, “\wj Who touched my clothes?\wj*”
\p
\v 31 \add But\add* his followers said, “You can see \add all the people\add* that were pressing on you \add so why would you ask\add* who touched \add you\add*?”
\p
\v 32 \add But\add* \add Yeshua\add* was \add still\add* looking around to see \add who\add* had done it
\v 33 \add when\add* the woman, \add scared and shaking because of what was happening\add*, came and fell \add to her knees\add* \add in front of\add* \add Yeshua\add* and told him the \add whole story\add*.
\v 34 “\wj Daughter, your faith has healed you,\wj*” \add Yeshua\add* said. “\wj Go in peace and \+add full health\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 35 While he was still speaking, \add messengers\add* came from \add the religious leader’s\add* house to tell \add Yair\add* \add (Jairus)\add*, “Your daughter has died. Why bother the teacher any more?”
\p
\v 36 But \nd Yeshua\nd* overheard them telling \add that\add* to the leader and told \add him\add*, “\wj Don’t be afraid—just keep believing.\wj*”
\v 37 \add Yeshua\add* didn’t allow anyone to accompany him other than Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add*, and Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and his brother, Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add*.
\v 38 As they approached \add Yair’\add* house, \add Yeshua\add* saw a \add big\add* commotion \add ahead of them\add*, with lots of wailing and crying \add going on\add*.
\v 39 As he entered, he said, “\wj Why are you all crying \+add in distress\+add*? The child hasn’t died—she’s \+add just\+add* sleeping!\wj*”
\p
\v 40 \add But\add* they \add just\add* ridiculed \add Yeshua\add*, \add so\add* he \add sent them all outside\add*, \add just\add* taking the father and mother of the child, \add along with three\add* with him. He went in where the \add girl\add* was,
\v 41 and taking \add her\add* hand, he said, “\wj Young woman, I tell you: get up!\wj*”
\v 42 Immediately \add she\add* got up and walked around, and \add everyone\add* marvelled \add at the amazing thing that had happened\add*. (She was twelve years old.)
\v 43 \add Yeshua\add* \add repeatedly\add* told them \add to keep this to themselves\add*, and \add added\add* that \add they\add* should give her \add something\add* to eat.
\c 6
\s1 Yeshua’s community can’t believe he’s from God
\r (Mat. 13:53-58; Luke 4:16-30)
\p
\v 1 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add left\add* \add Kafarnaoum\add* \add (Capernaum)\add* and \add went back with his followers\add* to \add Nazaret\add* \add (Nazareth)\add* \add ,\add* his \add birthplace\add*.
\v 2 \add It was now\add* the Rest Day and when he started teaching in the \add Jewish meeting hall\add*, many who heard him were astonished, saying, “Where did that man learn all that? \add How could he have such\add* wisdom and \add be able to do those\add* miracles?
\v 3 Isn’t that the carpenter, the son of Maria \add (Mary; Heb. Miryam; Grk. Maria/Mariam)\add*, and the brother of Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yosef \add (Joseph)\add* CHECK and Yehudah \add (Judas; Grk. Yudas)\add* and Shim’on \add (Simon)\add*? \add Don’t his sisters live around\add* here?” And they were offended by his \add teaching\add*.
\p
\v 4 Then \nd Yeshua\nd* told them, “\wj A prophet is \+add only dishonoured\+add* in his \+add own\+add* home town, and among his \+add own\+add* relatives, and in his \+add own\+add* home.\wj*”\x + \xo 6:4: \xt Yhn 4:44.\x*
\p
\v 5 He wasn’t able to do \add even\add* one miracle there, except for \add placing\add* his hands on a few sick \add people\add* and healing them.
\v 6 He \add was amazed at how they wouldn’t believe him as\add* he went around the villages teaching.
\s1 Yeshua sends his apprentices out in pairs
\r (Mat. 10:5-15; Luke 9:1-6)
\p
\v 7 Then he called his twelve \add apprentices\add* and started sending them out \add in pairs\add* and giving them authority over \add demons\add*.
\v 8 He \add insisted\add* that they \add can carry\add* a walking stick, but not to take \add food\add*, a backpack, or money.
\v 9 \add They could wear one pair of\add* sandals, \add but not take changes of\add* clothes,
\v 10 and he told them, “\wj Whenever you’re \+add invited\+add* into a home, stay \+add at that one place\+add* until you all \+add leave that town\+add*.\wj*
\v 11 \wj \+add But if any places don’t want you or don’t want to hear what you have to say\+add*, \+add just\+add* \+add leave that place\+add*. \+add As you go,\+add* shake the dust off your \+add sandals\x + \xo 6:11: \xt Acts 13:51.\x* so they can see\+add* \+add that you pass the responsibility of your leaving, onto them\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 12 \add So\add* \add the apprentices\add* went off and \add started\add* telling \add people\add* to repent.
\v 13 \add In addition,\add* they \add drove\add* out many demons, and anointed many sick \add people\add* with olive oil and healed them.\x + \xo 6:13: \xt Jam 5:14.\x*
\s1 The execution of Yohan-the-immerser
\r (Mat. 14:1-12; Luke 9:7-9)
\p
\v 14 \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* was \add now becoming well known\add* and King Herodes \add (Herod)\add* \add Antipas\add* heard about him. \add He thought that maybe\add* Yohan-the-immerser had \add come back to life\add* and that’s why \add Yeshua\add* \add was able to do\add* miracles.\x + \xo 6:14-15: \xt Mat 16:14; Mrk 8:28; Luk 9:19.\x*
\p
\v 15 But others \add thought it was\add* \add the promised return of\add* Eliyah \add (Elijah)\add*, and \add yet\add* others \add thought he must be\add* \add another\add* prophet like the \add ones\add* \add in the Scriptures\add*.
\p
\v 16 But hearing \add about Yeshua\add*, Herodes was \add telling people\add*, “That Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* who I \add had\add* beheaded, \add he must have come back to life\add*!”
\v 17 Because Herodes himself had had Yohan arrested and \add put\add* in prison because he had married Herodias, his brother Filippos’s \add (Philip)\add* wife.\x + \xo 6:17-18: \xt Luk 3:19-20.\x*
\v 18 Yohan had been telling \add the king\add* that it was wrong for \add him\add* to \add marry\add* \add his\add* brother’s wife,
\v 19 and \add so\add* Herodias resented him \add enough to\add* want to kill him, but \add Herodes\add* hadn’t be able to
\v 20 because \add he\add* respected Yohan as a righteous and holy \add teacher\add* and \add so\add* \add he kept him alive\add*. He \add often\add* enjoyed hearing from \add Yohan\add* and \add thought a lot\add* \add about what he said\add*.
\p
\v 21 \add However,\add* an \add opportunity\add* came at Herodes’s birthday \add celebration\add*, when he \add threw a feast\add* for his \add top officials\add* and generals, and for the leaders in Galil.
\v 22 The daughter of Herodias came in and danced \add for them\add*, and the king and \add his party guests all enjoyed it\add*. \add So\add* the king said to the young woman, “\add Just\add* ask me \add for anything\add* and I’ll give it to you.”
\v 23 Then he promised her, “\add Even if you asked for\add* half of my kingdom, I’d give it to you!”
\p
\v 24 \add So\add* she went out and \add asked\add* her mother \add what she should ask for\add*. \add Her mother\add* told \add her that she should ask for\add* Yohan’s head.
\p
\v 25 \add So\add* going back into \add the party\add*, she said seriously to the king, “I would like the head of Yohan-the-immerser \add right now\add* on a plate!”
\p
\v 26 The king \add was really upset\add* \add with that\add*, \add but\add* because \add he’d made loud promises in front of all his guests\add*, he \add couldn’t say no\add*.
\v 27 \add So\add* \add he\add* \add ordered\add* an executioner \add to go out and return with\add* \add Yohan’s\add* head. He \add went off and\add* beheaded him in the prison
\v 28 and brought \add the\add* head \add into the party\add* on a plate and gave it to the girl, and \add she\add* gave it to her mother.
\v 29 \add When\add* \add Yohan’s\add* followers heard \add about that\add*, they came and fetched his \add body\add* and \add put\add* it into a tomb.
\s1 Yeshua feeds 5,000 people
\r (Yhn 6:1-14; Mat. 14:13-21; Luke 9:10-17)
\p
\v 30 \add Now\add* the apprentices \add who had been sent out,\add* \add returned\add* back to \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add*, and they reported \add back\add* everything they had done and \add what they had been teaching\add* \add people\add*.
\v 31 Then he told them \add to head to\add* a quiet place \add with him to take a break\add*. \add That was\add* because there were \add so many people always\add* coming and going, and \add sometimes\add* they didn’t even have \add a chance\add* to eat.
\v 32 \add So\add* they went away by boat to a quiet place by themselves.
\p
\v 33 \add But\add* \add people from towns all around\add* had seen them going and recognised \add who they were, so\add* they ran \add around the lake\add* on foot and \add got there\add* ahead of them.
\v 34 \add So\add* when \add Yeshua\add* got out \add of the boat\add*, he saw a big crowd and \add felt sorry\add* for them because they \add seemed like\add* sheep without a shepherd,\x + \xo 6:34: \xt Num 27:17; 1Ki 22:17; 2Ch 18:16; Eze 34:5; Mat 9:36.\x* \add so\add* he started teaching them many \add things\add*.
\v 35 Then, when it was already getting late, his apprentices came up and said, “This place is \add pretty isolated\add* and it’s already late.
\v 36 Send \add these people\add* off \add now\add* so they can go to the \add nearby\add* settlements and villages and buy themselves something to eat.”
\p
\v 37 But \add Yeshua\add* answered them, “\wj You give them something to eat.\wj*”
\p They \add complained\add*, “\add If we go\add*, should we buy \add several months wages worth of bread\add* so we can give \add all of\add* them something to eat?”
\p
\v 38 \add But\add* he asked, “\wj Go \+add and find out\+add* how \+add much bread\+add* you all have.\wj*”
\p \add When they’d found out\add* they said, “Five \add buns\add* and two fish.”
\p
\v 39 \add Yeshua\add* \add told\add* all the people to \add line up\add* in rows \add and\add* sit down on the green grass.
\v 40 \add So\add* they sat down in rows of \add fifty to a hundred\add*.
\v 41 Then \add holding\add* the five buns and two fish, he looked up to the sky and blessed \add God\add*, and then broke up the buns and gave \add pieces\add* to his apprentices so they could \add do likewise\add* to \add the people\add*, and he \add also\add* divided up the two fish,
\v 42 and all \add the people\add* ate and were satisfied.
\v 43 Then they collected the leftover pieces \add of bread\add*, filling twelve baskets, \add as well as the leftover pieces\add* of fish.
\v 44 The \add headcount of\add* men who ate \add that evening\add* was five thousand.
\s1 Yeshua walks on the lake surface
\r (Yhn 6:15-21; Mat. 14:22-33)
\p
\v 45 \add Straight after that,\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add sent\add* his apprentices \add off\add* in the boat to go \add across\add* to Beyt-Tsayda while he sent the crowd \add home\add*.
\v 46 Then he said \add goodbye\add* to \add everyone\add*, \add and\add* \add climbed\add* the hill to pray.
\v 47 \add Later in the night,\add* the boat was out in the middle of the lake, and only \add Yeshua\add* remained back there on the land.
\v 48 He saw them \add struggling\add* to row \add against\add* the wind, and \add some time after 3am\add* he came \add out\add* to them, walking on the lake \add surface\add* \add as if to walk\add* past them.
\v 49 \add But\add* they had seen \add someone\add* walking on the lake \add and thought\add* it was a ghost, and they yelled out
\v 50 because they had all seen it and were \add terrified\add*.
\p \add But\add* \add Yeshua\add* immediately spoke to them and told them, “\wj \+add Hey,\+add* \+add take heart\+add*, \+add it’s me\+add*, don’t be afraid!\wj*”
\v 51 Then he \add climbed\add* up into the boat and the wind died down. They were all \add totally astounded\add*
\v 52 because they hadn’t understood \add the implications of him feeding all the people\add* because their \add minds were closed\add*.
\s1 Yeshua heals many people around Gennaisaret
\r (Mat. 14:34-36)
\p
\v 53 \add After completing their crossing\add*, they anchored at Gennaisaret.
\v 54 \add When\add* they got out of the boat, \add again\add* \add people\add* recognised \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add*
\v 55 and ran around that \add region\add*, \add so next minute\add* \add people\add* began \add bringing all of\add* those \add who\add* were sick, carrying them on pallets to wherever they heard that \add Yeshua\add* was.
\v 56 \add After that,\add* whenever \add Yeshua\add* entered villages or cities, or fields or marketplaces, they laid \add the sick\add* \add down there\add* and were imploring him that they might even just touch the \add edge\add* of his \add robe\add*, and anyone who \add did so\add* was healed.
\c 7
\s1 Yeshua suggests obeying God, not tradition
\r (Mat. 15:1-9)
\p
\v 1 \add Some from\add* the Farisaios party and some of the law teachers had come from Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* \add to observe\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add*
\v 2 and \add noticed\add* that some of his followers were eating \add their food\add* \add without following their religious customs, i.e.,\add* \add without washing their\add* hands.
\v 3 (The Farisaios and, \add in fact,\add* all the Jewish \add religious leaders\add* don’t eat without \add first ceremonially\add* washing \add their\add* hands \add as taught by their\add* elders \add over the generations\add*.
\v 4 They won’t eat at the market if they can’t do that \add first\add*, and have many other \add regulations about\add* \add ceremonial\add* \add washing\add* of cups and jugs and copper containers.)
\p
\v 5 Then the Farisaios and \add religious teachers\add* asked \add Yeshua\add*, “\add How come\add* your followers don’t \add respect\add* our \add Jewish\add* \add traditions\add*, but eat \add without the ceremonial washing of\add* hands?”
\p
\v 6 “\wj Yeshayah \+add (Isaiah)\+add* \+add got it exactly right\+add*,\wj*” he answered, “\wj \+add when he expressed\+add* \+add God’s thoughts\+add* about you hypocrites \+add and wrote\+add*:\wj*
\q1 \wj ‘These people honour me with \+add their\+add* lips,\wj*
\q2 \wj but their \+add real desires\+add* are far away from me.\wj*
\q1
\v 7 \wj \+add Their worship\+add* of me is worthless—\wj*
\q2 \wj teaching \+add man-made rules as if they are from God\+add*.’\wj*\x + \xo 7:6-7: \xt Isa 29:13 (LXX).\x*
\p
\v 8 \wj \+add You’ve ignored\+add* \nd God’s\nd* \+add commands\+add* \+add instead accepting\+add* human \+add traditions\+add*.\wj*
\p
\v 9 “\wj You all \+add simply\+add* dismiss \nd God’s\nd* \+add commands\+add* in \+add favour of\+add* your own customs,\wj* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* continued.
\v 10 \wj Mosheh \+add (Moses)\+add* \+add teaches\+add* \+add us\+add*,\wj*
\q1 \wj ‘Honour your \+add parents\+add*,’\wj*\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Exo 20:12; Deu 5:16.\x*
\q1 \wj and\wj*
\q1 \wj ‘Anyone \+add dishonestly slandering\+add* \+add their parents\+add* \+add deserves the death penalty\+add*.’\wj*\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Exo 21:17; Lev 20:9.\x*
\m
\v 11 \wj But \+add when you all encourage people\+add* to say, ‘Whatever I had that may have helped \+add you guys\+add* \+add has been given\+add* \+add to God\+add*’,\wj*
\v 12 \wj you are \+add actively discouraging\+add* them \+add from helping their parents\+add*—\wj*
\v 13 \wj \+add overriding\+add* \nd God’s\nd* message with your \+add very convenient\+add* \+add teaching that you disseminate instead\+add*. And \+add that’s not the only example\+add*!\wj*”
\s1 Evil comes from inside a person
\r (Mat. 15:10-20)
\p
\v 14 \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* called out to the crowd, “\wj \+add Everyone listen to me carefully\+add*:\wj*
\v 15 \wj Nothing that enters \+add your mouth\+add* \+add makes you guilty in God’s eyes\+add*. It’s what comes \+em out\+em* of \+add you\+add* \+add that demonstrates your culpability\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 16 ◘
\v 17 When \add Yeshua\add* came \add back inside\add*, his apprentices asked him \add what he meant\add*.
\v 18 “\wj \+add Can’t you understand something so simple\+add*,\wj*” he \add scolded\add* them. “\wj \+add Can’t you see\+add* that anything from the outside that enters \+add your body\+add* \+add doesn’t make you guilty in God’s sight\+add*,\wj*
\v 19 \wj because it doesn’t enter your \+add mind\+add* but \+add merely\+add* \+add goes into\+add* \+add your\+add* stomach and \+add ends up\+add* in the toilet.\wj*” (\add By saying this he clearly showed that\add* \add it was ok\add* \add for Yehudim\add* \add (Jews)\add* \add to eat\add* any food.)
\p
\v 20 “\wj It’s what comes out of \+add you\+add* that \+add makes you guilty in God’s eyes\+add*,\wj*” he \add continued\add*.
\v 21-22 “\wj That’s because evil thoughts, \+add sexual immorality, theft, murder, adultery,\+add* greed, wickedness, deceit, arrogance, lust, slander, pride, and foolishness all come from \+em inside\+em* people’s \+add hearts\+add* \+add and minds\+add*.\wj*
\v 23 \wj \+add So\+add* it’s the \+add evil\+add* that’s inside \+add a person\+add* and comes out that \+add makes them guilty\+add* \+add in God’s eyes\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 The bold faith of a non-Jewish woman
\r (Mat. 15:21-28)
\p
\v 24 \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* left \add that place\add* and went \add up north\add* into the regions of Tsor \add (Tyre)\add* and Tsidon \add (Sidon)\add*. He \add tried\add* to enter a house \add without being noticed\add* but \add didn’t succeed\add*,
\v 25 and straight away a woman who had heard about him \add turned up\add*. \add She knelt in front of\add* him because she had a \add young\add* daughter who was \add demon-possessed\add*.
\v 26 The woman was Greek from Foinikai in Aram \add (Syria)\add*, and she begged \add Yeshua\add* to \add command\add* the demon \add to leave\add* her daughter.
\v 27 “\wj Let the \+add Jewish\+add* children be \+add treated\+add* first,\wj*” he told her, “\wj because it’s not good to take the children’s food and \+add give\+add* it to the \+add household\+add* dogs.\wj*”
\p
\v 28 “Yes, \nd master\nd*,” she responded, “but the \add puppies\add* under the table \em do\em* get to eat the little crumbs that the children \add drop\add*.”
\p
\v 29 “\wj \+add Ha,\+add* go home \+add now\+add*\wj*” he answered, “\wj \+add As a result of how you just spoke\+add*, the demon has \+add already\+add* left your daughter.\wj*”
\p
\v 30 And when she \add got\add* home, the demon had \add indeed gone\add* and the \add young\add* girl was lying \add quietly\add* on \add her\add* bed.
\s1 Yeshua heals a deaf man who couldn’t speak
\p
\v 31 \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* left the Tsor \add (Tyre)\add* \add region\add*, passed through Tsidon \add (Sidon)\add*, and came down the \add eastern\add* side of Galil Lake to the Dekapolis \add region\add*.
\v 32 \add The people there\add* brought a man to him \add who couldn’t hear or speak\add*, and asked \add Yeshua\add* \add to heal\add* him.
\v 33 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* took \add the man\add* back \add away\add* from the crowd, put his fingers in \add the man’s\add* ears, then he spat and touched the man’s tongue.
\v 34 Looking up to the sky, he sighed and said, “\wj Open up!\wj*”
\p
\v 35 \add Then the man could hear\add*, and his tongue was released and he \add began to\add* speak properly.
\v 36 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add advised that they shouldn’t tell anyone\add*, but \add the more he said that\add*, \add the more they seemed to spread it around\add*.
\v 37 \add The crowds\add* were totally amazed, saying, “He \add can do anything\add*—he makes the deaf able to hear, and \add enables those who couldn’t speak\add*.”
\c 8
\s1 Yeshua feeds 4,000 people
\r (Mat. 15:32-39)
\p
\v 1 \add Another time\add* there was a large crowd again with nothing to eat. \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* called his apprentices and told them,
\v 2 “\wj I feel \+add sorry\+add* for \+add all these people\+add* because they’ve already been with us for three days and haven’t had anything to eat.\wj*
\v 3 \wj I can’t send them home because they’re \+add too weak to walk\+add*, and \+add some have a long way to go\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 4 “Where could anyone \add find enough food\add* \add out\add* here in the wilderness?” his apprentices \add queried\add*.
\p
\v 5 “\wj How \+add much bread\+add* have you all got?\wj*” he asked.
\p “Seven \add buns\add*,” they \add answered\add*.
\p
\v 6 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* instructed the crowd to sit down on the ground. Then he took the seven buns, gave thanks and \add pulled them apart\add*, giving \add pieces\add* to his apprentices to \add then distribute to\add* the crowd.
\v 7 They also had a few small \add cooked\add* fish, so he blessed them \add too\add* and got them \add to distribute\add* them \add as well\add*.
\v 8 After \add all the people\add* had eaten and were full, they collected seven basketfuls of \add leftovers\add*.
\v 9 \add There were some four thousand people there\add* \add that day\add*, and \add Yeshua\add* sent them \add home\add* \add after\add* they’d eaten.
\v 10 Then he \add and\add* his apprentices climbed into the boat and \add headed for\add* the Dalmanoutha \add region\add*.
\s1 The religious leaders want to see a miracle
\r (Mat. 16:1-4)
\p
\v 11 \add Some men from\add* the Farisaios \add party\add* came out \add to Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and started arguing with him. They were \add checking him out\add* \add and wanted to see him do a miracle\add*.\x + \xo 8:11: \xt Mat 12:38; Luk 11:16.\x*
\v 12 \add Yeshua\add* \add grieved inside and asked\add*, “\wj Why do \+add you people need to see a miracle\+add* \+add before you’ll believe me\+add*? \+add Actually, no miracle will be done for\+add* this generation.\wj*”\x + \xo 8:12: \xt Mat 12:39; Luk 11:29.\x*
\p
\v 13 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add left in the boat\add* again and \add crossed to the other side of the lake\add*.
\s1 The apprentices miss the significance of what’s happening
\r (Mat. 16:5-12)
\p
\v 14 \add But\add* \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add apprentices\add* forgot to take \add any food\add* other than one bun that \add someone in the boat had\add*.
\v 15 He told them, “\wj Watch out for the yeast of the Farisaios\x + \xo 8:15: \xt Luk 12:1.\x* and of \+add King\+add* Herodes \+add (Herod)\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 16 \add They asked each other what it meant—was it because they forgot food?\add*
\p
\v 17 \add But\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* knew \add what they were saying\add* and \add asked\add*, “\wj Why are you all discussing about not having \+add food\+add*? \+add Can’t you figure it out\+add*? \+add Or are your minds completely closed\+add*?\wj*
\v 18 \wj You all have eyes \+add but can’t seem to see\+add* and have ears \+add but can’t seem to listen\+add*.\x + \xo 8:18: \xt Jer 5:21; Eze 12:2; Mrk 4:12.\x* \+add Have you already\+add* \+add forgotten\+add* \+add what just happened\+add*?\wj*
\v 19 \wj When I broke up the five buns to feed five thousand \+add people\+add*, how many basketfuls of leftovers did you collect?\wj*”
\p “Twelve,” they answered.
\p
\v 20 “\wj And when we fed four thousand with seven buns, how many full baskets of leftovers \+add then\+add*?\wj*”
\p “Seven,” they \add answered\add*.
\p
\v 21 “\wj \+add So\+add* how can you all \+add fail to understand\+add* \+add what’s going on right in front of you\+add*,\wj*” \add Yeshua\add* \add asked\add*.
\s1 Yeshua heals a blind man near Beyt-Tsayda
\p
\v 22 \add As they entered\add* Beyt-Tsayda, \add the people\add* brought a blind \add man\add* to \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and asked him to touch him.
\v 23 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* took the man’s hand and led him out of the village. Then he spat in his eyes, placed his hands on him, and asked him, “\wj Can you see anything?\wj*”
\p
\v 24 The man looked \add around and answered\add*, “I can see the people, \add but they just look like\add* trees.”
\v 25 \add Yeshua\add* touched the man’s eyes again and then he could see clearly—\add he was now completely better\add*.
\v 26 Then \add Yeshua\add* told him not to go back into the village \add but to go straight\add* home.
\s1 Yeshua asks who they think he is
\r (Mat. 16:13-20; Luke 9:18-21)
\p
\v 27 Then \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and his apprentices \add moved around\add* the \add various\add* villages of Kaisareia-Filippi \add (Caesarea Philippi)\add*. On the way, he asked \add them\add*, “\wj Who \+add does everyone think I am\+add*?\wj*”
\p
\v 28 “\add Some say\add* Yohan-the-immerser,” they said, “some \add say\add* Eliyah \add (Elijah)\add*, \add and some\add* \add say\add* one of the prophets.”\x + \xo 8:28: \xt Mrk 6:14-15; Luk 9:7-8.\x*
\p
\v 29 “\wj And what do you all \+add think\+add*?\wj*” he asked.
\p “You are the \add promised one\add* \add sent by God\add*,” Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* answered him.\x + \xo 8:29: \xt Yhn 6:68-69.\x*
\p
\v 30 Then \add Yeshua\add* warned them \add not to tell others\add* about him.
\s1 Yeshua’s radical challenge to his would-be followers
\r (Mat. 16:21-28; Luke 9:22-27)
\p
\v 31 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* began teaching \add his apprentices\add* that the son of humanity would need to suffer a lot, to be rejected by \add the religious leaders\add*, and so to be \add put to death\add* \add but to come back to life\add* after three days.
\v 32 He taught this \add very\add* clearly, \add but\add* Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* took him aside \add and told him off\add*.
\v 33 \add Yeshua\add* turned back and \add looked at the others\add*, then reprimanded Kefa, “\wj \+add Stand back\+add*, Satan—you’re \+add applying human values instead of considering \nd God’s\nd* plan\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 34 Calling out to them and to the crowd, he said, “\wj Anyone who wants to follow me must first put aside their own desires and then follow me—even through very difficult times.\wj*\x + \xo 8:34: \xt Mat 10:38; Luk 14:27.\x*
\v 35 \wj Anyone who \+add worries about\+add* saving their own life will lose it, but anyone who \+add gives their life due to following\+add* me and \+add my\+add* \+add teaching\+add* will save \+add their life\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 8:35: \xt Yhn 12:25; Mat 10:39; Luk 17:33.\x*
\v 36 \wj \+add No, it doesn’t benefit\+add* a person if they gain \+add everything in\+add* the world yet lose their soul.\wj*
\v 37 \wj What can \+add someone offer in order to buy a home for\+add* their soul?\wj*
\v 38 \wj \+add Yes,\+add* anyone who’s ashamed of me and my \+add message\+add* \+add in front of\+add* this adulterous and sinful generation, the son of humanity will likewise be ashamed of them when he comes \+add clearly displaying his father’s greatness\+add* \+add and bringing\+add* the holy messengers.\wj*”
\c 9
\p
\v 1 Then he continued, “\wj I \+add can assure\+add* you that some of the ones standing here \+add won’t die\+add* until they’ve seen \nd God’s\nd* \+add powerful\+add* kingdom arrive.\wj*”
\s1 Mosheh and Eliyah speak with Yeshua
\r (Mat. 17:1-13; Luke 9:28-36)
\p
\v 2 Six days \add later\add*, \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* took Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* and Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add*, and \add just the four of them went\add* up onto a high hill. Then he was transformed \add right in front of their eyes\add*\x + \xo 9:2-7: \xt 2Pe 1:17-18.\x*
\v 3 and his clothes \add turned\add* incredibly shining white—\add whiter than any bleach could make them\add*.
\v 4 Then Eliyah \add (Elijah)\add* and Mosheh \add (Moses)\add* \add appeared beside\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* and \add started\add* talking with him.
\v 5 Kefa said \nd to Yeshua\nd*, “Teacher, it’s good that we’re here. Maybe we could make three shelters \add up here\add*: one for you, one for Mosheh, and one for Eliyah?”
\v 6 \add He said that\add* because they were terrified \add and\add* didn’t know what to \add say\add*.
\p
\v 7 Then a cloud shadowed them \add from the sun\add*, and a voice came out of the cloud \add saying\add*, “This is my dear son. \add Listen\add* to him.”\x + \xo 9:7: \xt Mat 3:17; Mrk 1:11; Luk 3:22.\x*
\v 8 \add When\add* they looked around, they couldn’t see anyone \add else there\add* anymore, except for \nd Yeshua\nd* \add himself\add*.
\p
\v 9 As they came down the hill \add again\add*, \add Yeshua\add* told them not to tell anyone what had happened up there until \add after\add* the son of humanity \add had come back to life\add*.
\p
\v 10 \add They remembered that, although between all three of them they couldn’t understand the bit about coming back to life\add*,
\v 11 \add so\add* they asked \add Yeshua\add*, “\add Isn’t\add* \add it written\add* that Eliyah will be the first \add to return\add*?”\x + \xo 9:11: \xt Mal 4:5; Mat 11:14.\x*
\p
\v 12 “\wj \+add Yes,\+add*\wj*” he \add answered\add*, “\wj Eliyah \+add (Elijah)\+add* is indeed the one to come first to \+add start\+add* \+add the restoration\+add*. But \+add isn’t\+add* it also written that the son of humanity will be despised and will suffer a lot?\wj*
\v 13 \wj \+add You see,\+add* Eliyah has come \+add already\+add*, and they \+add treated him just however\+add* they liked, \+add just\+add* like it was written \+add that it would happen\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua drives out a stubborn demon
\r (Mat. 17:14-21; Luke 9:37-43a)
\p
\v 14 When they got \add back\add* to \add his\add* \add other\add* followers, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* saw that \add they were surrounded by\add* a large crowd and the \add religious teachers\add* were debating with them.
\v 15 The crowd were very surprised when they \add noticed\add* \add Yeshua\add* and \add came\add* running to greet him.
\v 16 He asked them, “\wj What were you all arguing with them about?\wj*”
\p
\v 17 One of the \add people\add* answered, “Teacher, I brought my son here—\add he has a demon that prevents him from speaking\add*.
\v 18 Whenever it \add takes hold\add* of him, it attacks him and he starts foaming \add at the mouth\add* and grating his teeth and \add his joints lock up\add*. I \add tried to get\add* your followers to \add command it to leave but\add* they couldn’t.”
\p
\v 19 “\wj You’re a faithless generation,\wj*” \add Yeshua\add* replied. “\wj \+add How much longer\+add* will I \+add have to be here\+add*? \+add How much longer can\+add* I tolerate you all? Bring him \+add here\+add*.\wj*”
\v 20 \add So\add* they brought \add the boy\add* to him. \add When\add* he saw \add Yeshua\add*, the \add demon\add* immediately \add caused him to have\add* convulsions and fall on the ground—rolling \add over\add* and foaming \add at the mouth\add*.
\p
\v 21 \add Yeshua\add* asked \add the boy’s\add* father, “\wj How \+add long has this been happening for\+add*?\wj*”
\p “\add Since he was small\add*,” he \add replied\add*,
\v 22 “and often it throws him into the fire or into \add water\add* \add to try\add* to destroy him. But if \add can do anything\add* and you feel \add sorry\add* for us, \add please\add* help us.”
\p
\v 23 \nd Yeshua\nd* asked him, “\wj If \+add I\+add* can? A \+add person\+add* who believes \+add can do anything\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 24 The \add boy’s\add* father cried out, “I do believe—help me \add to fight\add* unbelief.”
\p
\v 25 Then \nd Yeshua\nd* \add noticing\add* that a \add big\add* crowd \add was quickly forming\add*, scolded the \add evil\add* spirit, “\wj \+add You spirit who causes muteness and deafness\+add*, \+add leave\+add* \+add this boy\+add* \+add now\+add* and \+add never return to\+add* him.\wj*”
\p
\v 26 \add There was yelling and strong convulsions\add*, and then the demon left him and \add the boy\add* \add lay still\add* as if dead, and many \add people\add* \add thought\add* he \add was\add*.
\v 27 \add However\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* took his hand \add and lifted it\add*, and \add the boy\add* got up.
\p
\v 28 When \add Yeshua\add* and his apprentices had gone into the house by themselves, they asked him, “\add How come\add* we couldn’t drive it out?”
\p
\v 29 “\wj That kind \+add will\+add* \+add only\+add* \+add leave after\+add* prayer and fasting,\wj*” he \add replied\add*.
\s1 Yeshua talks again about being executed
\r (Mat. 17:22-23; Luke 9:43b-45)
\p
\v 30 \add Then they left that place and were moving around\add* Galil, because \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* didn’t want \add people\add* to know where he was
\v 31 \add while\add* he was teaching his apprentices. He told them, “\wj The son of humanity will be arrested and \+add executed\+add*, \+add but\+add* after three days he’ll \+add come back to life\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 32 \add But\add* they didn’t know \add what that meant\add*, and they were \add too scared\add* to ask him.
\s1 How to be the best
\r (Mat. 18:1-5; Luke 9:46-48)
\p
\v 33 Then they went to Kafarnaoum \add (Capernaum)\add* and \add when they arrived at\add* the house, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* asked them what they were \add discussing\add* on the way.
\p
\v 34 \add But they\add* \add didn’t reply\add* because while they were walking, they’d been \add talking about which of them\add* is the best.\x + \xo 9:34: \xt Luk 22:24.\x*
\v 35 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* sat down \add and\add* called the twelve \add of them\add* and \add explained\add*, “\wj Anyone who wants to be \+add at the top\+add*, has to be \+add at the bottom and help all the others\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 9:35: \xt Mat 20:26-27; 23:11; Mrk 10:43-44; Luk 22:26.\x*
\v 36 Then \add Yeshua\add* called a \add young boy\add* \add and\add* stood him in the middle of them, and \add giving him a hug\add* said,
\v 37 “\wj Anyone who \+add welcomes young\+add* children \+add on my behalf\+add*, \+add welcomes\+add* me, and anyone who \+add welcomes\+add* me is not \+add actually\+add* \+add welcoming\+add* me, but \+add welcoming\+add* the one who sent me \+add here\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 9:37: \xt Yhn 13:20; Mat 10:40; Luk 10:16.\x*
\s1 Others are also serving Yeshua
\r (Luke 9:49-50)
\p
\v 38 Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* \add checked with\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add*, “Teacher, we saw someone \add using your authority\add* to \add command demons to leave\add*, \add but\add* we \add told him off\add* because he wasn’t \add one of\add* us.”
\p
\v 39 \nd Yeshua\nd* \add responded\add*, “\wj \+add No, don’t stop\+add* him, because \+add anyone\+add* who does a miracle \+add using\+add* my name \+add won’t\+add* just quickly \+add turn around and\+add* \+add slander\+add* me.\wj*
\v 40 \wj \+add Yes,\+add* anyone who’s not against us is for us.\wj*\x + \xo 9:40: \xt Mat 12:30; Luk 11:23.\x*
\v 41 \wj \+nd Anyone\+nd* who gives you water to drink because you’re \+add followers\+add* \+nd of\+nd* \+add God’s\+add* \+nd chosen\+nd* \+nd one\+nd* \+add and who does it because they’re working for me\+add*, I \+add can assure\+add* you that they’ll \+add receive\+add* their reward.\wj*\x + \xo 9:41: \xt Mat 10:42.\x*
\s1 Difficult teachings about disobedience
\r (Mat. 18:6-9; Luke 17:1-2)
\p
\v 42 “\wj \+add But\+add* anyone who \+add causes\+add* a \+add young person\+add* to \+add falter from their trust\+add* in me, it would be better if they were thrown into the sea with a heavy \+add weight tied\+add* around their neck.\wj*
\v 43 \wj If your hand \+add causes you to disobey God\+add*, cut it off—it’s better to enter \+add eternal\+add* life being maimed, than to have two hands \+add but to be thrown\+add* into the fire \+add that never goes out\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 9:43: \xt Mat 5:30.\x*
\v 44 ◘
\v 45 \wj And if your foot \+add causes you to disobey God\+add*, cut it off—it’s better to enter \+add eternal\+add* life being maimed, than to have two feet but to be thrown into \+add hell\+add*.\wj*
\v 46 ◘
\v 47 \wj And if your eye \+add causes you to disobey God\+add*, \+add gouge\+add* it out—it’s better to enter \nd God’s\nd* kingdom one-eyed, than to have two eyes and be thrown into \+add hell\+add*\wj*\x + \xo 9:47: \xt Mat 5:29.\x*
\v 48 \wj where the \+add worms\+add* never die and the fire \+add never goes out\+add*.\wj*
\p
\v 49 “\wj Everyone will be salted with fire.\wj*
\p
\v 50 “\wj \+add Now\+add* salt is good, but if \+add it\+add* \+add were to go bad\+add*, what would you season \+add your food\+add* with \+add then\+add*?\x + \xo 9:50: \xt Mat 5:13; Luk 14:34-35.\x* \+add So keep yourselves like\+add* salt, and \+add strive to get on well\+add* with each other.\wj*”
\c 10
\s1 It’s God that joins husband and wife
\r (Mat. 19:1-12; Luke 16:18)
\p
\v 1 Then \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* left \add Kafarnaoum\add* \add (Capernaum)\add* and went down to the Yehudah \add (Judea)\add* area and \add across\add* the Yarden \add (Jordan)\add* \add river\add*. Again the crowds \add followed\add* him, and he taught them \add just like he usually did\add*.
\p
\v 2 Some from the Farisaios party approached \add Yeshua\add* \add to check him out and\add* asked, “\add Does the law allow\add* a husband to dismiss \add his\add* wife?”
\p
\v 3 “\wj \+add Well\+add*, what \+add law\+add* did Mosheh \+add (Moses)\+add* \+add give to\+add* you all?\wj*” he \add asked\add*.
\p
\v 4 They \add answered\add*, “Mosheh \add said that a husband is allowed\add* to write a \add statement\add* of divorce and dismiss \add his wife with it\add*.”\x + \xo 10:4: \xt Deu 24:1-4; Mat 5:31.\x*
\p
\v 5 “\wj \+add Yes,\+add* he wrote that law,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add responded\add*, “\wj \+add because he saw\+add* your \+add stubborn desires\+add*,\wj*
\v 6 \wj but \+add God\+add* made \+add both\+add* \+add men and women\+add* \+add right\+add* at the beginning.\wj*\x + \xo 10:6: \xt Gen 1:27; 5:2.\x*
\v 7 \wj \+add As a result\+add*, a man leaves his \+add parents\+add* and joins together with his wife\wj*\x + \xo 10:7-8: \xt Gen 2:24.\x*
\v 8 \wj and the \+add couple become a single unit\+add*. So there’s no longer two \+add of them\+add*, but \+add only\+add* one.\wj*
\v 9 \wj \+add So if it’s\+add* \+nd God\+nd* who joins them together \+add like that\+add*, \+add no person\+add* \+add has the authority\+add* to separate them.\wj*”
\p
\v 10 \add Back\add* in the house again, \add his\add* apprentices asked about that,
\v 11 and \add Yeshua\add* told them, “\wj Anyone who \+add divorces\+add* his wife and marries another \+add person\+add*, \+add commits adultery towards\+add* \+add his wife\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 10:11-12: \xt Mat 5:32; 1Cor 7:10-11.\x*
\v 12 \wj And \+add likewise,\+add* if \+add the wife\+add* \+add divorces\+add* her husband \+add and\+add* marries another \+add person\+add*, she’s committing adultery \+add towards her husband\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua encourages childlike faith
\r (Mat. 19:13-15; Luke 18:15-17)
\p
\v 13 \add The people\add* were bringing small children for \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* to touch, but \add his\add* apprentices scolded them.
\v 14 However, \nd Yeshua\nd* \add noticed\add* \add it\add* \add and was upset\add*, “\wj \+add Just\+add* let \+add those kids\+add* come. Don’t prevent them, because \nd God’s\nd* kingdom \+add consists of people like them\+add*.\wj*
\v 15 \wj \+add Actually\+add*, you can’t \+add even\+add* \+add enter\+add* \nd God’s\nd* kingdom \+add unless you accept it just like a small child does\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 10:15: \xt Mat 18:3.\x*
\v 16 \add So he continued hugging\add* \add the children\add* and \add commanding a good life for\add* them as he placed his hands on \add each one\add*.
\s1 Leaving everything behind to be saved
\r (Mat. 19:16-30; Luke 18:18-30)
\p
\v 17 \add One time when\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* was starting out on a trip, a man caught up to him and kneeling down \add in front\add* of him asked, “Good teacher, what do I have to do to inherit eternal life?”
\p
\v 18 “\wj Why do you call me \+em good\+em*?\wj*” \add he\add* \add asked\add*. “\wj No \+add person\+add* is good—only \+nd God\+nd* \+add is\+add*.\wj*
\v 19 \wj You know \+add God’s\+add* \+add instructions\+add*: don’t murder,\x + \xo 10:19: \xt Exo 20:13; Deu 5:17.\x* don’t commit adultery,\x + \xo 10:19: \xt Exo 20:14; Deu 5:18.\x* don’t steal,\x + \xo 10:19: \xt Exo 20:15; Deu 5:19.\x* don’t \+add lie in court\+add*,\x + \xo 10:19: \xt Exo 20:16; Deu 5:20.\x* don’t defraud \+add others\+add*, and honour your \+add parents\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 10:19: \xt Exo 20:12; Deu 5:16.\x*
\p
\v 20 “Teacher, I’ve kept all of those since I was young,” \add the man\add* \add responded\add*.
\p
\v 21 \nd Yeshua\nd* \add looked up at him with genuine love\add* and said, “\wj \+add There’s one thing still to be done\+add*: sell \+add everything\+add* you have and give \+add the money\+add* to the poor—then you’ll have \+add wealth\+add* in heaven. \+add After that,\+add* come and follow me.\wj*”
\v 22 But \add the man\add* \add grew very sad when he heard that\add*, and he went away upset because he \add owned\add* many properties.
\p
\v 23 \nd Yeshua\nd* looked around and told his followers, “\wj \+add It’s so difficult for wealthy people\+add* to enter \nd God’s\nd* kingdom.\wj*”
\p
\v 24 (\add His\add* followers \add were a bit stunned at his teaching\add*.) \nd Yeshua\nd* \add continued\add*, “\wj \+add Yes\+add*, it’s \+add certainly\+add* difficult to enter into \nd God’s\nd* kingdom.\wj*
\v 25 \wj It’s easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for a rich \+add person\+add* to enter \nd God’s\nd* kingdom.\wj*”
\p
\v 26 \add Now\add* they were \add totally stunned\add*, \add asking\add*, “\add How can anyone possibly be saved then?\add*”
\p
\v 27 \nd Yeshua\nd* \add looked intently at\add* them, “\wj \+add Yes,\+add* \+add humanly\+add* it’s \+add quite\+add* impossible. But with \+nd God\+nd* \+add it’s different—God can do anything\+add*!\wj*”
\p
\v 28 Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* said, “\add Well\add*, we left everything \add and came\add* and followed you.”
\p
\v 29 “\wj \+add Yes, I can assure\+add* you all,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add answered\add*, “\wj that \+add anyone\+add* who left \+add their\+add* home or \+add farm\+add*, and \+add left\+add* \+add their\+add* \+add siblings or parents\+add* or children because of me and my \+add teaching\+add*,\wj*
\v 30 \wj they’ll \+add be\+add* \+add rewarded\+add* one hundred times over with homes and farms and \+add siblings and parents\+add* and children along with \+add times of persecution\+add*, \+add but gaining eternal life in the next era\+add*.\wj*
\v 31 \wj But many \+add at the top now\+add* will be \+add at the bottom then\+add*, and \+add many\+add* \+add at the bottom now will be blessed then\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 10:31: \xt Mat 20:16; Luk 13:30.\x*
\s1 Yeshua’s third prediction about his execution
\r (Mat. 20:17-19; Luke 18:31-34)
\p
\v 32 They were \add heading south\add* on \add their\add* way to Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* with \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add in front\add*, and \add his followers\add* were \add a bit surprised and a bit scared\add*. \add Yeshua\add* took the twelve \add aside\add*, and started telling them \add what\add* was going to happen to him,
\v 33 “\wj We’re on our way \+add down\+add* to Yerushalem and the son of humanity will be turned over to the chief priests and the \+add religious teachers\+add*, and they’ll \+add sentence him to be executed\+add* and hand him over to the \+add non-Jews\+add*.\wj*
\v 34 \wj Then they’ll ridicule him and spit on him \+add before\+add* they beat him and execute him, \+add but he’ll come back to life again in\+add* three days \+add time\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 How to become respected in God’s kingdom
\r (Mat. 20:20-28)
\p
\v 35 Then Zavday’s \add (Grk. Zebedaios)\add* two sons, Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add*, approached \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add and asked\add*, “Teacher, \add we’d like to ask a favour from you—please\add* \add don’t disappoint us\add*.”
\p
\v 36 “\wj What do you want \+add from me\+add*?\wj*” \add Yeshua\add* \add asked\add*.
\p
\v 37 They \add answered\add*, “\add Allow\add* us \add two\add* to sit \add beside you in heaven\add*—one \add of us on each side\add* of you.”
\p
\v 38 “\wj You don’t \+add even\+add* \+add understand\+add* what you’re asking for,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add replied\add*. “\wj Do you think you \+add could endure the suffering that I have to go through\+add*? Or to be \+add enveloped in the darkness that I have to go down into\+add*?\wj*”\x + \xo 10:38: \xt Luk 12:50.\x*
\p
\v 39 “\add Sure we can\add*,” they \add replied\add*.
\p “\wj \+add And indeed you all will suffer like me and be enveloped in darkness like I will be\+add*,\wj*” \add responded\add* \nd Yeshua\nd*,
\v 40 “\wj but \+add as for deciding who will sit next to\+add* me, \+add that’s not my decision to make because it’s already been decided\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 41 When the ten \add other apprentices\add* heard \add what those two had asked for\add*, they \add were upset at\add* Ya’akov \add (Jacob)\add* and Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add*.
\v 42 \add But\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* called them \add over\add*, “\wj \+add Listen,\+add* \+add in most countries their rulers boss the people around and their leaders\+add* exert their authority over them.\wj*\x + \xo 10:42-43: \xt Luk 22:25-26.\x*
\v 43 \wj But it \+add doesn’t work like\+add* that with you—anyone of you who wants to be \+add honoured\+add* must \+add serve the others\+add*,\wj*\x + \xo 10:43-44: \xt Mat 23:11; Mrk 9:35; Luk 22:26.\x*
\v 44 \wj and anyone who wants to become the \+add most respected\+add* has to \+add work\+add* \+add like a slave does\+add*.\wj*
\v 45 \wj Even the son of humanity didn’t come to be served, but to serve \+add others\+add* and to give his life as a ransom \+add to set many people free\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Blind Bar-Timaios gets his miracle
\r (Mat. 20:29-34; Luke 18:35-43)
\p
\v 46 They arrived at Yeriho \add (Jericho)\add*, and then \add when\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and his apprentices were leaving \add again\add* with a large crowd following, \add they came across\add* blind Bar-Timaios \add (Grk. Bartimaios)\add* (Timaios’ son) sitting beside the path \add begging\add*.
\v 47 \add When\add* he heard that it was \nd Yeshua\nd* from Nazaret \add going past\add*, he \add yelled\add* out, “\nd Yeshua\nd*, \add promised\add* descendant of David, \add help me please\add*.”
\p
\v 48 When \add several people told him to stop\add*, he \add just yelled out even louder\add*, “\add Yeshua, promised\add* descendant of David, \add please help me\add*.”
\p
\v 49 Then \nd Yeshua\nd* stopped and \add got the people to call\add* \add the blind man\add*. \add So\add* they called him, “\add Hey,\add* be \add confident\add*! Get up \add and come because\add* he’s called for you.”
\p
\v 50 \add So\add* \add Bar-Timaios\add* threw off his jacket, jumped up, \add and\add* \add was led\add* to \nd Yeshua\nd*.
\p
\v 51 “\wj \+add Now,\+add* what do you want me to do for you?\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add asked\add*.
\p “My teacher, \add I’d like to be able to see\add*,” \add Bar-Timaios\add* \add replied\add*.
\p
\v 52 “\wj \+add Okay,\+add* \+add off you go\+add* \+add then\+add*,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add responded\add*. “\wj Your faith has saved you.\wj*”
\p Immediately \add Bar-Timaios\add* \add was able to see\add*, and followed along the path after \add Yeshua\add*.
\c 11
\s1 Yeshua is treated like a king entering Yerushalem
\r (Yhn 12:12-19; Mat. 21:1-11; Luke 19:28-40)
\p
\v 1 As they got close to Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* and were passing Beyt-Fagey \add (Bethphage)\add* and Beyt-Ania \add (Bethany)\add* on the Mt. of Olives, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* sent two of his apprentices \add ahead\add*.
\v 2 telling them, “\wj Go on to the \+add next\+add* village and \+add as\+add* you enter it, you’ll \+add see\+add* a \+add young donkey\+add* that \+add hasn’t ever been ridden yet\+add*. Untie it and bring it \+add back here\+add*.\wj*
\v 3 \wj If anyone \+add asks\+add* what you’re doing, tell \+add them\+add* that the \+nd master\+nd* needs it and he’ll \+add return it later\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 4 \add So\add* they went \add ahead\add* and found a donkey tied up on the path \add just\add* outside the door of a house, and \add so they went to\add* untie it.
\v 5 \add But\add* some of the \add people\add* standing around there said, “\add Hoy!\add* What \add do you think\add* you’re doing untying \add that\add* donkey?”
\p
\v 6 \add So\add* they \add responded\add* \add just\add* as \nd Yeshua\nd* had told \add them\add*, and \add the people\add* allowed them \add to proceed\add*.
\v 7 They brought the \add young donkey\add* to \nd Yeshua\nd*, placing their coats over it \add before\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add mounted\add* it.
\v 8 \add As Yeshua rode it into Yerushalem,\add* many \add people\add* laid their coats on the road, while others lay down leafy branches cut \add from trees\add* in \add nearby\add* fields.
\v 9 \add Some went ahead and others came along behind\add*, shouting, “\add This is the saviour who comes with the authority and blessing from\add* \nd Yahweh\nd*\x + \xo 11:9: \xt Psa 118:25-26.\x*—
\v 10 the \add promised\add* ancestor of \add King\add* David who is blessed \add as he ushers in\add* his kingdom—\add the blessed\add* saviour \add from heaven\add*.”
\p
\v 11 And \add so\add* \add Yeshua\add* arrived in Yerushalem and went into the temple and looked \add all\add* around, \add but\add* \add because it was now\add* evening, he went back out to Beyt-Ania \add (Bethany)\add* \add village\add* \add (Bethany)\add* with \add his\add* twelve \add apprentices\add*.
\s1 Yeshua curses a fig tree
\r (Mat. 21:18-19)
\p
\v 12 The next day \add after they’d left\add* Beyt-Ania \add (Bethany)\add* \add village\add* \add (Bethany)\add*, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add was hungry\add*.
\v 13 \add From a distance he noticed\add* a fig tree \add that was in leaf\add* \add so\add* he \add went over to see if there was any fruit\add* on it, \add but\add* \add when he reached\add* it \add there was only\add* leaves because it wasn’t the \add right\add* season for figs.
\v 14 \add So he spoke\add* to \add the tree\add*, “\wj \+add No one in this\+add* age will \+add ever\+add* eat fruit from you \+add again\+add*.\wj*” (His followers \add heard\add* \add him say that\add*.)
\s1 Yeshua upsets the traders inside the temple
\r (Yhn 2:13-22; Mat. 21:12-17; Luke 19:45-48)
\p
\v 15 Then they came \add back\add* into Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* and on into the temple where \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* started driving out the \add sellers\add* and the \add buyers\add* \add that were trading\add* in \add there\add*. Then he \add tipped over\add* the money-changers’ tables and the chairs of the ones selling doves,
\v 16 and \add stopped others from carrying goods\add* through the temple.
\v 17 He taught them, “\wj Isn’t it written \+add in the Scriptures\+add*,\wj*
\q1 \wj ‘My house will be \+add known as\+add* a prayer house for all the nations \+add to use\+add*’?\wj*\x + \xo 11:17: \xt Isa 56:7.\x*
\m \wj But all of you have \+add turned it into a sanctuary for swindlers\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 11:17: \xt Jer 7:11.\x*
\p
\v 18 \add When\add* the chief priests and the \add religious teachers\add* heard that, they \add started\add* \add looking for\add* a way that they could destroy him, because they were afraid of him \add and the way that\add* the whole crowd marvelled at his teaching.
\p
\v 19 \add Every\add* evening, \add Yeshua and his apprentices\add* would go out of the city \add to stay overnight\add*.
\s1 Yeshua gives a lesson on moving mountains
\r (Mat. 21:20-22)
\p
\v 20 \add As they entered the city again\add* in the morning, \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add apprentices\add* \add noticed\add* that the fig tree \add was totally dead\add*.
\v 21 Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* remembered \add what he had said to the tree\add*, \add and\add* \add commented\add*, “\add Teacher\add*, \add that\add* fig tree that you cursed has withered up.”
\p
\v 22 “\wj \+add Use\+add* your faith \+add in\+add* \+nd God\+nd*,\wj* \nd Yeshua\nd* responded.
\v 23 \wj \+add I can assure\+add* you all that if anyone tells a mountain to go away into the sea, and doesn’t doubt in their \+add mind\+add* but believes that what they’re saying will happen, \+add then\+add* it will.\wj*\x + \xo 11:23: \xt Mat 17:20; 1Cor 13:2.\x*
\v 24 \wj \+add So\+add* I tell you all that anything you ask \+add God\+add* for \+add in your prayers\+add*, if you believe that you have received it, \+add then you will\+add*.\wj*
\v 25 \wj \+add All of you,\+add* whenever you’re standing praying, if you have something against someone, be \+add sure\+add* to forgive them so that your father in \+add heaven\+add* can also forgive your \+add disobedience\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 11:25-26: \xt Mat 6:14-15.\x*
\s1 The leaders question Yeshua’s authority
\r (Mat. 21:23-27; Luke 20:1-8)
\p
\v 26 ◘
\v 27 They \add continued on\add* into Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* and \add on to\add* the temple where they \add were met by\add* the chief priests and the \add religious teachers\add* and the elders.
\v 28 They \add asked\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add*, “Did you have any authority to do \add what you did\add*? \add If so,\add* who gave \add it\add* to you?”
\p
\v 29 “\wj \+add Okay,\+add* I’ll also ask you \+add something\+add*,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add replied\add*, \wj and \+add when you all\+add* answer me, I’ll tell you \+add about\+add* \+add my\+add* authority to do that:\wj*
\v 30 \wj When Yohan \+add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\+add* \+add preached and\+add* \+add immersed\+add* \+add people\+add*, did the authority for that come from heaven or from \+add people here\+add*?\wj*”
\p
\v 31 They \add discussed\add* that among themselves, reasoning, “If we say it was from heaven, he’ll ask us why \add we\add* didn’t believe him \add then\add*.
\v 32 But we \add can’t\add* say that it was just from \add people\add*.” (They said that because they were scared of the \add crowds\add*, \add knowing that\add* they believed that Yohan really was a prophet.)
\v 33 \add So\add* they answered, “We don’t know.”
\p “\wj \+add Well then,\+add*\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add responded\add*, “\wj I won’t tell you about \+add my\+add* authority to do those \+add things\+add* \+add either\+add*.\wj*”
\c 12
\s1 The parable about the tenants killing the owner’s son
\r (Mat. 21:33-46; Luke 20:9-19)
\p
\v 1 Then he started telling them \add some\add* parables: “\wj A man planted a vineyard and put a fence around it, dug out a \+add wine-pressing pit\+add*, and built a \+add security\+add* tower.\x + \xo 12:1: \xt Isa 5:1-2.\x* Then he rented it out and \+add went off\+add* travelling.\wj*
\v 2 \wj At \+add harvest time\+add*, he sent a slave \+add to go\+add* to the tenant farmers \+add and get his percentage of the harvest\+add*.\wj*
\v 3 \wj But \+add the tenants\+add* grabbed \+add the slave\+add* and beat him up, then sent him \+add back\+add* empty-handed.\wj*
\v 4 \wj \+add The owner\+add* sent \+add a second\+add* slave, but they \+add insulted\+add* that one and struck him on the head.\wj*
\v 5 \wj \+add So\+add* \+add the owner\+add* sent a \+add third\+add* \+add slave\+add* and they murdered \+add him\+add*. \+add He sent\+add* many other \+add slaves\+add*—some they \+add just\+add* beat up \+add and\+add* others they murdered.\wj*
\v 6 \wj \+add But\+add* \+add the owner\+add* still had \+add his\+add* one, dearly loved son, \+add so\+add* \+add finally\+add* he sent him to go, \+add thinking that they would now be convinced because\+add* it was \+add his\+add* son.\wj*
\v 7 \wj However, those tenant farmers said to \+add each other\+add*, ‘\+add Ah ha.\+add* This is the \+add one who will inherit\+add* \+add this land\+add*. \+add If\+add* we kill \+em him\+em*, \+add we’ll be the ones to control the estate\+add*.’\wj*
\v 8 \wj \+add So they\+add* took him and killed him, and threw \+add the body\+add* outside the vineyard \+add fence\+add*.\wj*
\p
\v 9 “\wj \+add Now\+add*, what \+add do you think\+add* the vineyard owner will do? \+add Yes,\+add* he’ll come and \+add eliminate\+add* \+add those\+add* \+add evil\+add* tenants, and give the \+add contract\+add* to others.\wj*
\v 10 \wj Haven’t you all read this in the \+add scriptures\+add*:\wj*
\q1 \wj ‘the stone that the \+add builders\+add* rejected\wj*
\q1 \wj became the \+add important\+add* cornerstone\wj*
\q1
\v 11 \wj that was given by \+nd Yahweh\+nd*,\wj*
\q1 \wj and \+add we think it’s incredible\+add*.’?\wj*”\x + \xo 12:10-11: \xt Psa 118:22-23.\x*
\p
\v 12 Then \add those leaders\add* tried to arrest him \add because\add* they knew that it was them that the parable was \add addressed at\add*, \add but\add* \add they couldn’t do it because Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add had the favour\add* of the crowd, so they \add just\add* left \add the area\add*.
\s1 Yeshua answers about paying taxes
\r (Mat. 22:15-22; Luke 20:20-26)
\p
\v 13 Then \add the religious leaders\add* sent some \add members\add* of the Farisaios party and \add some\add* of the \add political\add* supporters of \add King\add* Herodes \add (Herod)\add* \add to try to\add* catch \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add out\add*.
\v 14 \add So\add* they \add flattered\add* him, “Teacher, we know that you are \add honest even if it upsets others\add*, and that you teach the truth \add about\add* \nd God\nd* \add without caring about people’s opinions\add*. Is it \add right\add* \add for us Yehudim\add* \add (Jews)\add* to \add pay\add* the poll tax to \add the Romaios emperor\add* or not? \add How should we handle this\add*?”
\p
\v 15 \add However,\add* knowing their hypocrisy, \add Yeshua\add* \add responded\add* to them, “\wj Why are all of you \+add trying to\+add* test me? Bring me a \+add coin\+add* so I can see it.\wj*”
\p
\v 16 \add When\add* they brought \add him\add* \add a coin\add*, he \add asked\add*, “\wj Whose image and inscription \+add are on this\+add* \+add coin\+add*?\wj*”
\p “The \add emperor’s\add*,” they \add answered\add*.
\p
\v 17 “\wj \+add Well then,\+add*\wj*” said \nd Yeshua\nd*, “\wj give the \+add emperor whatever is due\+add* \+add him\+add*, \+add but\+add* \+add give\+add* \+nd God\+nd* \+add what is owed\+add* \+nd to\+nd* \+nd God\+nd*.\wj*”
\p \add After that,\add* they \add had to admit that that was an outstanding answer\add*.
\s1 Yeshua explains that those who’ve died are alive
\r (Mat. 22:23-33; Luke 20:27-40)
\p
\v 18 \add Another time\add*, \add members of\add* the Saddoukaios \add (Sadducee)\add* sect (which says that there’s no resurrection),\x + \xo 12:18: \xt Acts 23:8.\x* came to \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* and asked,
\v 19 “Teacher, Mosheh \add (Moses)\add* wrote that if a \add man’s\add* \add married\add* brother should die \add before\add* \add his\add* wife \add without having any\add* children, then his brother \add should marry\add* \add her\add* \add to produce descendants\add* \add in his brother’s name\add*.\x + \xo 12:19: \xt Deu 25:5.\x*
\v 20 \add Now what if\add* there were seven brothers and the first \add one\add* \add got married\add* and died \add childless\add*.
\v 21 \add So\add* then the second \add brother\add* took her in, \add but\add* \add again\add* died \add childless\add*, and then too the third.
\v 22 \add Eventually all\add* seven \add brothers\add* died \add childless\add*, and finally the woman also died.
\v 23 \add Now,\add* at the resurrection \add of the dead\add*, which \add brother\add* will she be the wife of, because \add at some point,\add* \add she was married to\add* \add each of\add* the seven \add of them\add*?”
\p
\v 24 “\wj \+add Actually you’re all quite wrong\+add*,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add answered\add*, “\wj because \+add you ignore\+add* the scriptures and \+add also\+add* \+add because you haven’t experienced\+add* \nd God’s\nd* power.\wj*
\v 25 \wj When the dead \+add do come back to life\+add*, they won’t be getting engaged or married, but will be like the messengers in the heavens.\wj*
\v 26 \wj But \+add as for the state of those who’ve died\+add*, didn’t you all read in the \+add scriptures about\+add* Mosheh \+add when\+add* \+nd God\+nd* spoke to him \+add in front of\+add* the \+add burning\+add* thorn bush and said, ‘I \+em am\+em* the \+nd god\+nd* of Avraham and the \+nd god\+nd* of Yitshak \+add (Isaac)\+add* and the \+nd god\+nd* of Ya’akov’ \+add (Jacob)\+add*?\wj*\x + \xo 12:26: \xt Exo 3:6.\x*
\v 27 \wj \+add So\+add* \+add God\+add* is not the \+nd god\+nd* of the dead, but of the living. You \+add Saddoukaios\+add* \+add (Sadducees)\+add* are \+add very wrong\+add*!\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua answers about genuine obedience to God
\r (Mat. 22:34-40; Luke 10:25-28)
\p
\v 28 Then one of the \add religious teachers\add* who had heard their \add question and\add* \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add excellent answer\add*, \add came closer\add* \add and\add* asked, “Which of \add God’s\add* \add commands\add* is the \add most important\add*?”
\p
\v 29 “\wj \+add Well\+add*,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* answered, “\wj the \+add most important\+add* is \+add this\+add*: ‘\+add Listen\+add*, Yisrael \+add (Israel)\+add*. Our \+nd God Yahweh\+nd* is \+add our\+add* \+nd master\+nd*.\wj*
\v 30 \wj You \+add must love\+add* \+nd Yahweh God\+nd* with all your heart and all your soul, and with all your mind and all your strength.’\wj*\x + \xo 12:29-30: \xt Deu 6:4-5.\x*
\v 31 \wj \+add And\+add* the second is: ‘Love your neighbour like \+add you look after\+add* yourself.’\x + \xo 12:31: \xt Lev 19:18.\x* \+add There’s\+add* \+add no other\+add* \+add commands\+add* \+add more important\+add* than these.\wj*”
\p
\v 32 The teacher \add replied\add* to \add Yeshua\add*, “\add Yes\add*, teacher, \add you’re quite right\add* saying there’s \add only\add* one \add God\add* and no other,\x + \xo 12:32: \xt Deu 4:35.\x*
\v 33 and \add saying that\add* \add we should\add* love him with all \add our\add* heart and all \add our\add* intelligence and all \add our\add* strength, and to be loving \add our\add* \add neighbours\add* like we \add look after\add* \add ourselves\add*, \add and all this\add* is more important than all the \add required temple\add* offerings and sacrifices.”\x + \xo 12:33: \xt Hos 6:6.\x*
\p
\v 34 \add When\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* saw that he’d \add given such a thoughtful answer\add*, he said, “\wj You’re \+add very close to\+add* \+nd God’s\+nd* kingdom!\wj*”\x + \xo 12:28-34: \xt Luk 10:25-28.\x*
\p \add After that,\add* no one \add else\add* dared to ask \add Yeshua\add* \add any more questions\add*.
\s1 Yeshua asks about the messiah being David’s descendant
\r (Mat. 22:41-46; Luke 20:41-44)
\p
\v 35 \add Later when\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* was teaching in the temple, \add he asked\add* \add the people\add*, “\wj How is it that the teachers \+add here\+add* say that the \+nd messiah\+nd* is a descendant of \+add King\+add* David?\wj*
\v 36 \wj \+add Because\+add* David himself said \+add under the inspiration of\+add* the holy \+nd spirit\+nd*,\wj*
\q1 \wj ‘\+nd Yahweh\+nd* told my \+nd master\+nd*,\wj*
\q2 \wj “Sit there \+add in the position of honour\+add*\wj*
\q2 \wj until I can \+add conquer\+add* your enemies.” ’\wj*\x + \xo 12:36: \xt Psa 110:1.\x*
\m
\v 37 \wj \+add If\+add* David calls \+add the messiah\+add* his \+nd master\+nd*, \+add how can\+add* \+add the messiah\+add* \+add possibly be\+add* \+add David’s\+add* descendant?\wj*”
\p The large crowd \add was very interested to hear everything that\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add had to say\add*.
\s1 Yeshua warns about well-dressed teachers
\r (Mat. 23:1-36; Luke 20:45-47)
\p
\v 38 \add As\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add continued teaching\add*, he said, “\wj Watch out for those \+add religious teachers\+add* \+add who like to wear\+add* \+add fancy\+add* robes and be greeted in the \+add square\+add*,\wj*
\v 39 \wj and \+add have the\+add* best seats \+add at meetings\+add* and the best places at dinners.\wj*
\v 40 \wj \+add Those people\+add* \+add trick widows out of their properties\+add*, \+add but offer\+add* long prayers \+add to cover it up\+add*. They will be getting a stricter judgement \+add than others\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 A widow’s sacrificial donation
\r (Luke 21:1-4)
\p
\v 41 \add As\add* he sat down in front of the \add temple\add* treasury, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add watched\add* the crowd as they threw \add coins\add* into the \add dish\add*, and some rich \add people\add* were \add donating quite valuable silver coins\add*.
\v 42 Then an impoverished widow came \add and\add* threw \add in\add* two \add small copper coins\add*.
\v 43 \add Yeshua\add* called his followers and told them, “\wj \+add Honestly\+add*, that hard-up widow \+add gave\+add* more than all the \+add others\+add*.\wj*
\v 44 \wj \+add You see, most\+add* \+add people\+add* \+add donate from their excess\+add* wealth, but this woman \+add even\+add* \+add gave\+add* \+add some of\+add* \+add the small amount that she needed to live on\+add*.\wj*”
\c 13
\s1 Yeshua predicts the temple’s total destruction
\r (Mat. 24:1-2; Luke 21:5-6)
\p
\v 1 \add As\add* \add they\add* were leaving the temple \add area\add*, one of \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* followers \add noted\add*, “Teacher, look at those \add large, chiselled\add* stones and those \add beautiful\add* buildings \add that they’ve been made into\add*.”
\p
\v 2 “\wj \+add Yes, incredible\+add* buildings,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add responded\add*, “\wj \+add but\+add* \+add the time will come\+add* when they’re torn down—\+add not a single\+add* \+add piece of\+add* stone \+add will be left sitting in its place\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua talks about coming hardships
\r (Mat. 24:3-14; Luke 21:7-19)
\p
\v 3 \add Later when they were over\add* on the Mt. of Olives \add overlooking\add* the temple, Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* and Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* and Andreas were \add with\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add and\add* asked
\v 4 when all that \add destruction\add* would happen, and what \add indications there would be that it would be about to happen\add*.
\p
\v 5 But \nd Yeshua\nd* told them, “\wj Be \+add careful\+add* so you all aren’t misled \+add by others\+add*.\wj*
\v 6 \wj \+add Plenty\+add* \+add of people\+add* will say that they’re coming \+add because they were sent by me\+add*, or that \+add they\+add* \+em are\+em* \+add me\+add*, and they’ll mislead many \+add others\+add*.\wj*
\v 7 \wj Also, whenever you all hear about wars or \+add about\+add* battles \+add about to begin\+add*, don’t be worried—\+add those things will certainly happen\+add*, but \+add there’s more to follow\+add*.\wj*
\v 8 \wj \+add Countries\+add* will \+add take up arms\+add* against \+add other\+add* \+add countries\+add*, and \+add kingdoms\+add* against \+add other\+add* \+add kingdoms\+add*. There’ll be earthquakes in \+add many\+add* places and there’ll be famines, \+add but\+add* those \+add will be just like\+add* the beginning of birth pains.\wj*
\p
\v 9 “\wj \+add So be careful\+add*. You’ll be \+add turned\+add* over to \+add local\+add* councils \+add for questioning\+add*, will be \+add whipped\+add* in the \+add Jewish meeting halls\+add*, and will be stood \+add in front of\+add* governors and kings \+add because of following\+add* me. \+add However, you’ll be able to present your life stories\+add* to them\wj*\x + \xo 13:9-11: \xt Mat 10:17-20; Luk 12:11-12.\x*
\v 10 \wj and it’s right that the good message first\wj*\f + \fr 13:10 \ft TD: It’s not clear here what was meant by ‘first’—‘first’ before what?\f* \wj be proclaimed to \+add every people group\+add*.\wj*
\v 11 \wj But whenever they take you all \+add along to\+add* hand you over, don’t worry \+add in advance\+add* \+add about\+add* what you’re going to say \+add to defend yourselves\+add*, but \+add wait until the hearing proceeds and speak what you are given then\+add*, because then it won’t be you speaking, but \+add God’s\+add* \+nd spirit\+nd*.\wj*
\v 12 \wj \+add In those times,\+add* a brother will \+add report on\+add* \+add his\+add* brother to \+add have him executed\+add*, and a father \+add report on\+add* his child, and children \+add will be encouraged to report on\+add* \+add their\+add* \+add own\+add* parents and then they’ll be \+add executed\+add* \+add as a result\+add*.\wj*
\v 13 \wj Then every one will hate you all because \+add they hate\+add* my name, but anyone who endures to the end will be saved.\wj*\x + \xo 13:13: \xt Mat 10:22.\x*
\s1 Yeshua warns about coming horror and deceptions
\r (Mat. 24:15-28; Luke 21:20-24)
\p
\v 14 “\wj But whenever you all see the \+add most horrible thing that drives people\+add* \+add from God\+add*, standing where it shouldn’t be\x + \xo 13:14: \xt Dan 9:27; 11:31; 12:11.\x* (\+add and you\+add* \+add readers should understand that\+add*), then anyone in Yehudah \+add (Judea)\+add* should flee into the hills,\wj*
\v 15 \wj and anyone \+add upstairs\+add* \+add looking outside\+add* shouldn’t come down into \+add the bedrooms\+add* to get anything,\wj*\x + \xo 13:15-16: \xt Luk 17:31.\x*
\v 16 \wj and anyone \+add working outside\+add* shouldn’t go back \+add inside to get a change of clothes\+add*.\wj*
\v 17 \wj \+add It will be extremely difficult\+add* for \+add pregnant\+add* women and for \+add mothers\+add* who are breast-feeding \+add their children\+add* in those days.\wj*
\v 18 \wj \+add Just pray\+add* that it won’t happen in the winter,\wj*
\v 19 \wj because those days will be \+add terrible\+add* like \+add nothing that’s ever happened before\+add*, \+add all the way back to when\+add* \+nd God\+nd* created \+add the world, right\+add* until the present time, and \+add won’t ever happen\+add* \+add again\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 13:19: \xt Dan 12:1; Rev 7:14.\x*
\v 20 \wj If \+nd Yahweh\+nd* hadn’t shortened \+add that time\+add*, \+add no humans\+add* would \+add even survive\+add*, but he shortened \+add that time so that\+add* the chosen \+add ones\+add* \+add could be saved\+add*.\wj*
\p
\v 21 \wj \+add So\+add* don’t believe it if you all \+add hear\+add* someone say, ‘Look, the \+nd messiah\+nd* \+add has arrived\+add* here.’ or ‘There’s the \+nd one\+nd* \+add that God\+add* \+add has sent\+add*.’\wj*
\v 22 \wj \+add Plenty of\+add* fake messiahs and \+add deceiving\+add* prophets will \+add certainly\+add* \+add come\+add* and \+add even\+add* \+add do things that humans can’t normally do\+add*, \+add so much so\+add* that \+add even\+add* the chosen \+add ones\+add* \+add would defect if that were\+add* possible.\wj*
\v 23 \wj \+add So\+add* watch out, \+add but\+add* I’ve \+add warned\+add* you \+add in advance\+add* \+add about\+add* all \+add of that\+add*.\wj*
\s1 The universe collapses as the son arrives
\r (Mat. 24:29-31; Luke 21:25-28)
\p
\v 24 “\wj After those \+add very difficult times\+add*, the sun will \+add go dark\+add*\x + \xo 13:24: \xt Isa 13:10; Yoel 2:10,31; 3:15; Rev 6:12.\x* and the moon won’t \+add shine\+add* \+add at night\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 13:24: \xt Isa 13:10; Eze 32:7.\x*
\v 25 \wj The stars will fall \+add down\+add* out of the sky\x + \xo 13:25: \xt Isa 34:4; Rev 6:13.\x* and the powers in the heavens will be shaken \+add up\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 13:25: \xt Yoel 2:10.\x*
\v 26 \wj Then \+add the people\+add* will see the son of humanity in the clouds coming with incredible power and \+add brightness\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 13:26: \xt Dan 7:13; Rev 1:7.\x*
\v 27 \wj He’ll send the messengers out to collect all the chosen \+add people\+add* from the four \+add corners of the world\+add*—from \+add everywhere between\+add* the earth and the sky.\wj*
\s1 Watch out for the change in season
\r (Mat. 24:32-35; Luke 21:29-33)
\p
\v 28 “\wj \+add So\+add* learn a lesson from fig \+add trees\+add*—whenever the \+add branches\+add* \+add green up\+add* and \+add start\+add* sprouting leaves, then everyone knows that summer is close.\wj*
\v 29 \wj So too whenever you see all those \+add things\+add* happening, you know that \+add the end of this current world\+add* is close.\wj*
\v 30 \wj I \+add can assure\+add* you all that the generation \+add of people who see those things\+add* won’t \+add die off before\+add* those \+add latter\+add* things happen.\wj*
\v 31 \wj The sky and the planet \+add might collapse\+add*, but my \+add teachings\+add* will \+add never become irrelevant\+add*.\wj*
\s1 Stay alert for the coming of the master
\r (Mat. 24:36-44)
\p
\v 32 “\wj But as for the \+add date or time\+add* \+add when all that will happen\+add*, \+add only\+add* the father knows that—even the son and the messengers in heaven don’t \+add know\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 13:32: \xt Mat 24:36.\x*
\v 33 \wj \+add So\+add* watch out, \+add observe\+add* \+add current events\+add*, and be praying, because you won’t know \+add exactly\+add* when \+add all this will happen\+add*.\wj*
\v 34 \wj It \+add can all be compared to\+add* a man who \+add was about\+add* to leave his home and \+add go on a trip\+add*. \+add Before he leaves,\+add* he gives \+add certain\+add* \+add jobs and responsibilities\+add* to his \+add various\+add* slaves, and \+add instructs his security guard to stay alert\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 13:34: \xt Luk 12:36-38.\x*
\v 35 \wj So you all watch \+add and stay alert\+add*, because you don’t know when the master of the house \+add might return\+add*—\+add perhaps one\+add* evening or at midnight, or at \+add dawn\+add* or maybe \+add mid-\+add*morning.\wj*
\v 36 \wj You \+add certainly\+add* \+add don’t want to be caught napping\+add* \+add when\+add* he comes,\wj*
\v 37 \wj and what I’m telling all of you \+add now\+add*, I tell \+add everyone\+add*: \+add stay alert and\+add* watch.\wj*”
\c 14
\s1 The leaders plan to eliminate Yeshua
\r (Yhn 11:45-53; Mat. 26:1-5; Luke 22:1-2)
\p
\v 1 \add Now\add* it was two days \add before\add* the Passover Feast and the \it Flat Bread \+add Celebration\+add*\it*,\x + \xo 14:1: \xt Exo 12:1-27.\x* and the chief priests and the \add religious teachers\add* were \add trying to figure out\add* how they could have \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add set up so they could arrest him and have him executed\add*,
\v 2 \add but\add* they \add knew that the Feast wouldn’t be a good time because the people would protest\add* \add in Yeshua’s favour\add*.
\s1 The woman anoints Yeshua for his burial
\r (Yhn 12:1-8; Mat. 26:6-13)
\p
\v 3 \add Meanwhile,\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* was in Beyt-Ania \add (Bethany)\add* at the home of Shim’on \add (Simon)\add* who \add had previously\add* \add had leprosy\add*. \add Yeshua\add* was \add sitting\add* \add there when\add* a woman came \add in\add* with a \add hand-crafted container\add* of very expensive \add fragrant lotion\add*. Breaking \add open\add* the \add sealed\add* flask, she poured \add the fragrant oil\add* over \add Yeshua’s\add* head.\x + \xo 14:3: \xt Luk 7:37-38.\x*
\v 4 \add Immediately\add* some \add in the room started\add* \add quietly grumbling about the extravagant waste\add*,
\v 5 then they scolded \add the woman\add* because \add a flask of genuine\add* lotion like that could \add easily\add* \add fetch almost a year’s wages if\add* it was sold.
\p
\v 6 But \nd Yeshua\nd* \add spoke up\add*, “\wj \+add What do you think you’re all doing abusing\+add* her—leave her \+add alone\+add*! She’s done \+add something very good for\+add* me.\wj*
\v 7 \wj You’ll always have poor \+add people\+add* \+add around\+add*,\x + \xo 14:7: \xt Deu 15:11.\x* and you \+add can help\+add* them whenever you want to, but \+add I won’t be around forever\+add*.\wj*
\v 8 \wj She has \+add performed\+add* the \+add traditional\+add* anointing of my body \+add in advance\+add* of my burial,\wj*
\v 9 \wj and I \+add can assure\+add* you all, that wherever the good message is proclaimed \+add around\+add* the world, what \+add she\+add* has done \+add today\+add* will \+add be part of the story and she’ll be remembered for it\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Yehudah offers to hand Yeshua over
\r (Mat. 26:14-16; Luke 22:3-6)
\p
\v 10 Then Yehudah \add (Judas; Grk. Yudas)\add* Iskariot, one of \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* twelve \add apprentices\add*, \add visited\add* the chief priests \add to offer to hand\add* \add Yeshua\add* over to them.
\v 11 When they heard \add that\add*, they were \add very pleased\add* and promised to \add pay him well\add*, and \add Yehudah\add* \add asked them about the most convenient way for them to get hold of\add* \add Yeshua\add*.
\s1 Yeshua’s apprentices prepare the Passover meal
\r (Yhn 13:21-30; Mat. 26:17-25; Luke 22:7-14, 21-23)
\p
\v 12 On the first day of the \it Flat Bread \+add Celebration\+add*\it* when \add the lambs\add* \add would be slaughtered ready for the special Passover meal\add*, \add Yeshua’s\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* apprentices \add asked\add* him, “Where do you want \add us to get everything ready for our Passover meal\add*?”
\p
\v 13 \add So\add* \add Yeshua\add* sent off two of \add them\add* \add with these instructions\add*, “\wj Go into town and a man carrying a pitcher of water will meet you there. \+add Just\+add* follow him\wj*
\v 14 \wj \+add until\+add* he goes into \+add a house\+add*. Then \+add find\+add* the owner of the house and tell him that the teacher \+add wants to know\+add* \+add the location of\+add* the guestroom where he and his apprentices can celebrate \+add their\+add* Passover meal.\wj*
\v 15 \wj He’ll show you a large, furnished room \+add upstairs\+add*—\+add that’s where you can get everything ready\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 16 \add So\add* the \add two of them\add* went off into the town, and \add everything happened there\add* \add exactly\add* as \add Yeshua\add* had told them, and so they prepared the \add special meal\add* \add there\add*.
\s1 Yeshua shocks his apprentices at the Passover meal
\r (Yhn 13:21-30; Mat. 26:20-30; Luke 22:14-23; 1 Cor. 11:23-25)
\p
\v 17 As the evening \add approached\add*, \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* went in \add for dinner\add* with \add his\add* twelve \add apprentices\add*.
\v 18 \add As\add* they were sitting around eating, \add he\add* told them, “\wj I’ll tell you \+add frankly\+add* that one of you eating with me \+add here\+add* will hand me over \+add to be arrested\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:18: \xt Psa 41:9.\x*
\v 19 \add That upset them\add*, and \add several of them individually asked\add*, “Surely it couldn’t be me?”
\p
\v 20 Then he \add continued\add*, “\wj It’s one of \+add you\+add* twelve—the one who dips \+add his bread\+add* in the \+add sauce at the same time as\+add* me.\wj*
\v 21 \wj \+add Indeed\+add* it’s written \+add in the scriptures\+add* that the son of humanity will be arrested, but on the other hand, \+add what a tragedy it’ll be for\+add* the one who hands him over—\+add in fact\+add* it would be better for that man if he was never born.\wj*”
\p
\v 22 \add As\add* they \add carried on\add* eating, \add he\add* took \add some\add* bread, blessed \add God\add*, broke it \add apart\add* and gave \add a piece\add* to them, saying, “\wj Take this \+add bread\+add*—it’s my body.\wj*”
\p
\v 23 Then he picked up a cup, gave thanks \add to God\add*, \add and\add* \add passed it around so\add* they could \add each\add* drink from it,
\v 24 saying, “\wj That is the blood of my \+add contract\+add*\x + \xo 14:24: \xt Exo 24:8.\x* that will be poured out for many \+add people\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 14:24: \xt Jer 31:31-34.\x*
\v 25 \wj I can \+add assure\+add* you all that I won’t drink \+add anything made from grapes\+add* until I drink new \+add juice\+add* in \nd God’s\nd* kingdom.\wj*”
\p
\v 26 Then after they’d sung \add some\add* songs, they left \add the town\add* and went \add across\add* to the Mt. of Olives.
\s1 Yeshua predicts Peters denials
\r (Yhn 13:36-38; Mat. 26:31-35; Luke 22:31-34)
\p
\v 27 Then \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add continued\add* his \add teaching\add*, “\wj All of you will stumble because it’s written \+add in the scriptures\+add*: ‘I’ll strike \+add down\+add* the shepherd and the sheep will get scattered.’\wj*\x + \xo 14:27: \xt Zech 13:7.\x*
\v 28 \wj But after \+add I come back to life\+add*, I’ll go on ahead of you all \+add back\+add* to Galil.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:28: \xt Mat 28:16.\x*
\p
\v 29 \add But\add* Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* \add contradicted\add* him, “Even if everyone \add else\add* stumbles, I won’t!”
\p
\v 30 “\wj I can assure you,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add responded\add*, “\wj that you’ll renounce me three times this \+add very\+add* night, before the rooster crows \+add early tomorrow morning\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 31 But \add Kefa\add* argued forcibly, “\add Even if I had\add* to die with you, I would \add never\add* disown you!”
\p And all \add the others\add* said similar \add things\add*.
\s1 Yeshua, in distress, prays at Gethsaimanai
\r (Mat. 26:36-46; Luke 22:39-46)
\p
\v 32 They \add walked along until\add* they came to a \add piece of land called\add* Gethsaimanai where \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* told his apprentices to sit down while \add he\add* prayed.
\v 33 He took Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* and Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yohan \add (John; Grk. Yoannes)\add* \add further in\add* with him where he \add stared off in a daze\add* \add but\add* was \add obviously very\add* distressed.
\v 34 He told \add the three of\add* them, “\wj My soul is \+add deathly sad\+add*! \+add You guys just\+add* stay here and \+add keep alert\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 35 He went ahead a little \add way\add*, where he knelt on the ground \add with his head down\add* and prayed—\add asking\add* if it was possible to avoid \add what was ahead of\add* him.
\v 36 \add But\add* he said, “\wj Father, \+add I know that you can do anything\+add*. \+add Let me avoid this suffering\+add*, but \+add yes I do know, it doesn’t matter\+add* what I want but rather what you’ve \+add planned\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 37 Then he \add went back\add* and found the others sleeping. “\wj Shim’on \+add (Simon)\+add*, are you asleep?\wj*” he \add asked\add* Kefa. “\wj \+add Couldn’t you stay awake\+add* \+add even for\+add* a \+add single\+add* hour?\wj*
\v 38 \wj You all \+add need to\+add* \+add stay alert and be careful\+add* not to \+add give\+add* into temptation. \+add I know your spirits are enthusiastic\+add* on one hand, \+add but it’s still easy to give in to the moment\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 39 Then \add he went further in\add* \add again and\add* prayed \add as before\add*,
\v 40 \add but when he returned\add* again, he found them all asleep because \add they were tired\add*, \add but they couldn’t really find any excuse to give\add*.
\p
\v 41 The third time that \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* returned, he said to them, “\wj \+add Ah,\+add* you’re all sleeping again \+add and having\+add* a \+add good\+add* rest. It’s \+add well-earned\+add* \+add but\+add* look, the \+add time\+add* has come for the son of humanity to be \+add handed\+add* over to \+add evil men\+add*.\wj*
\v 42 \wj \+add Come on—get up\+add*—we \+add need\+add* to go! Look, the one who’ll hand me over \+add is almost here\+add*.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua is arrested in the night
\r (Yhn 18:3-12; Mat. 26:47-56; Luke 22:47-53)
\p
\v 43 \add Even while\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* was still speaking, Yehudah \add (Judas; Grk. Yudas)\add* (one of \add his\add* twelve \add apprentices\add*) \add reached him\add*, \add followed by\add* a crowd \add that included some of\add* the chief priests, the \add religious teachers\add*, and the \add Jewish\add* elders—\add many armed\add* with swords and clubs.
\v 44 \add Yehudah\add* had \add prearranged\add* a signal with them that the one \add he\add* \add greeted with a\add* kiss, \add they\add* should grab \add that person\add* and lead him away \add under guard\add*.
\p
\v 45 \add So he walked right up\add* to \add Yeshua\add* \add and\add* said, “My honoured teacher,” and \add greeted\add* him with a kiss.
\v 46 Then \add the others with him\add* \add grabbed\add* \add Yeshua\add* and secured him.
\v 47 But one of the ones \add with Yeshua\add* that was beside him, drew \add his\add* sword and struck one of the chief priest’s \add slaves\add*—cutting off the man’s ear.
\v 48 \nd Yeshua\nd* spoke to \add the crowd\add*, “\wj Did you all bring swords and clubs \+add to try\+add* to capture me \+add like you’d chase down\+add* a thief?\wj*
\v 49 \wj I was teaching \+add there\+add* in the temple every day\x + \xo 14:49: \xt Luk 19:47; 21:37.\x* and you could have arrested me, but \+add it’s happened this way\+add* \+add to ensure\+add* that \+add what’s written in\+add* scriptures will be fulfilled.\wj*”
\p
\v 50 \add Meanwhile,\add* \add the others who’d been with Yeshua\add* \add had taken off\add*.
\v 51 One young fellow was wearing a \add single\add* linen robe, and when \add the crowd\add* \add tried to\add* grab him,
\v 52 \add it came off\add* \add in the struggle\add* and he \add ran away\add* \add stark\add* naked.
\s1 The mock trial where Yeshua is sentenced to death
\r (Yhn 18:13-14,19-24; Mat. 26:57-68; Luke 22:54-55,63-71)
\p
\v 53 \add The guards\add* led \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* away to the chief priest’s \add residence\add*, and all the chief priests and the elders and the \add religious teachers\add* gathered \add there\add* \add also\add*.
\v 54 Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* followed along from a distance and went in as far as the courtyard of \add that residence\add*, where he \add joined\add* the servants who were sitting around the fire keeping warm.
\v 55 \add Inside,\add* the chief priests and all the council were \add trying to establish a case\add* against \nd Yeshua\nd* so he could be sentenced to death, but they weren’t \add coming up with anything\add*.
\v 56 Several people were \add making up charges\add* against him, but \add none of the accusers’ stories agreed with each other\add*.
\p
\v 57 \add Eventually\add* some of them stood up and \add offered\add* \add this\add* false \add charge\add*:
\v 58 “We heard him say that \add he\add* would demolish this temple \add made by many labourers\add*, and within three days \add he’d\add* build another \add one\add* \add without any helpers\add*.”\x + \xo 14:58: \xt Yhn 2:19.\x*
\v 59 \add But even then\add*, \add they couldn’t get their accusations to align with each other\add*.
\p
\v 60 \add Nevertheless,\add* the chief priest in the middle \add of the council\add* stood up and asked \nd Yeshua\nd*, “\add Aren’t you going to defend yourself\add*? These men are \add accusing you\add* \add of those things\add*.”
\p
\v 61 But \add Yeshua\add* \add didn’t say anything\add*, \add so\add* the chief priest asked again, “\add Is it true\add* that you’re the \nd chosen\nd* \add one\add* \add that God promised to send\add*—the son of the blessed \add God\add*?”
\p
\v 62 “\wj I am.\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* \add replied\add*, “\wj and you’ll all see the son of humanity sitting \+add in the honoured position\+add* by the \+add powerful\+add* \+add God\+add* and coming through the clouds in the sky.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:62: \xt Dan 7:13.\x*
\p
\v 63 Then the chief priest tore his own robe \add to show his disgust\add* and \add shouted\add*, “We \add certainly\add* \add don’t need any more\add* witnesses \add now\add*!
\v 64 You \add yourselves\add* all heard \add him insult\add* \add God\add*. What \add sentence does that deserve\add*?”
\p \add So\add* the \add leaders\add* there agreed that \add Yeshua\add* \add needed to be\add* \add sentenced to\add* death.\x + \xo 14:64: \xt Lev 24:16.\x*
\p
\v 65 Then \add various people\add* started spitting on him, and blindfolding him and beating him saying, “\add Ha,\add* \add tell us who that was\add*!” \add Even\add* the servants \add joined in\add* \add to slap him\add*.
\s1 Kefa disowns Yeshua
\r (Yhn 18:15-18,25-27; Mat. 26:69-75; Luke 22:56-62)
\p
\v 66 \add Meanwhile,\add* Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* was down in the courtyard \add when\add* one of the chief priest’s servant girls came \add outside\add*,
\v 67 and seeing Kefa warming himself, she looked more closely and said, “\add Hey,\add* you were with \add that\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* from Nazaret \add (Nazareth)\add*!”
\p
\v 68 But he denied it, “I don’t know him and I don’t know \add why you think I would\add*!” Then he \add moved away from the fire\add*.
\p
\v 69 \add But\add* the girl that had seen him said to \add some of the others\add* standing around, “That guy’s \add one\add* of them.”
\p
\v 70 But again \add Kefa\add* denied it.
\p A little while later, some of those standing there said \add the same thing\add* to \add him\add*, “You must \add be one of\add* them because you’re from Galil.”
\p
\v 71 \add Now\add* \add Kefa\add* started swearing and cursing \add and said\add*, “I’ve \add never even met that fellow\add* that you’re all talking about!”
\p
\v 72 Right then the rooster crowed for the second time and Kefa remembered \add now\add* what \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* had told him—\add how\add* \add he\add* would renounce \add Yeshua\add* three times before the rooster crowed—and he broke down \add and\add* cried.
\c 15
\s1 Pilatos tries to interrogate Yeshua
\r (Yhn 18:28-38; Mat. 27:1-2,11-14; Luke 23:1-5)
\p
\v 1 \add First thing\add* in the morning, the chief priests \add called a meeting\add* with the elders and the \add religious teachers\add* and all the council, and they ordered that \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* be tied up and taken over to \add Governor\add* Pilatos \add (Pilate)\add*.
\v 2 \add There\add* Pilatos asked him, “Are you the king of the Yehudim \add (Jews)\add*?”
\p “\wj You said it,\wj*” replied \add Yeshua\add*.
\p
\v 3 Then the chief priests \add started\add* \add hurling\add* \add accusations\add* against \add Yeshua\add*,
\v 4 \add so\add* Pilatos asked him again, “\add Don’t you have anything to say\add*? \add Listen to all those accusations they’re making\add* against you.”
\p
\v 5 \add But\add* Pilatos was astounded that \nd Yeshua\nd* didn’t answer any further.
\s1 Pilatos agrees to execute an innocent man
\r (Yhn 18:39–19:16; Mat. 27:15-26; Luke 23:13-25)
\p
\v 6 \add Now at time of\add* the \add Jewish\add* \add Passover\add*, at their request, \add Pilatos\add* \add (Pilate)\add* would \add normally\add* \add pardon\add* one prisoner for them.
\v 7 There was \add another prisoner at that time\add* named Bar-Aba \add (Grk. Barabbas)\add*, \add who was an activist arrested for\add* murder.
\v 8 \add By now the crowd had arrived\add*, and asked Pilatos \add to release a prisoner\add* as \add usual\add* \add at Passover\add*,
\v 9 \add so\add* \add he\add* \add asked\add* them, “Do you all want me to \add release\add* the King of the Yehudim \add (Jews)\add* for you?”
\v 10 (\add That was\add* because \add Pilatos\add* was \add well\add* aware that the chief priests had brought \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* because they were jealous \add of his popularity\add*.)
\v 11 But the chief priests stirred up the crowd \add to start saying\add* that it was Bar-Aba \add that they wanted released\add*,
\v 12 \add so\add* Pilatos asked again, “Then what should I do \add with\add* \add this man\add* that you call the King of the Yehudim?”
\p
\v 13 \add The crowd\add* yelled back, “Execute him on a post.”
\p
\v 14 “What has he \add even done wrong\add*?” Pilatos \add demanded\add*.
\p But they \add just\add* yelled \add louder\add*, “Execute him on a post!”
\p
\v 15 \add Now\add* Pilatos wanted to placate the crowd, so he had Bar-Aba released while he had \nd Yeshua\nd* flogged and then handed over \add to the execution squad\add*.
\s1 The battalion plays with their mock ‘king’
\r (Yhn 19:2-3; Mat. 27:27-31)
\p
\v 16 \add So\add* the soldiers led \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* inside the palace that was the governor’s residence, and called in \add the rest of\add* the battalion.
\v 17 They \add mocked Yeshua\add* by dressing him in a \add kingly\add* \add robe\add*, and after \add someone\add* twisted some thorns together into a \add mock\add* crown, they \add pressed it onto his head\add*,
\v 18 and began saluting him, “Greetings, king of the Yehudim \add (Jews)\add*.”
\v 19 They \add took turns\add* whacking his head with a stick and spitting on him, \add while\add* \add others\add* knelt down \add in front of\add* him and \add pretended\add* to be bowing to him.
\v 20 \add After they’d finished having fun\add* mocking him, they took the purple robe off him, and put his own robe \add back\add* on him. Then they led him outside \add towards the execution area\add*.
\s1 Yeshua is publicly executed beside thieves
\r (Yhn 19:17-27; Mat. 27:32-44; Luke 23:26-43)
\p
\v 21 \add As they walked out of the city,\add* they \add came across\add* a man coming in from the country. \add He was\add* Shim’on \add (Simon)\add* from Kurainai \add (Cyrene)\add* \add (Kurainai\add*—the father of Alexandros \add (Alexander)\add* and Rufos),\x + \xo 15:21: \xt Rom 16:13.\x* and \add the soldiers\add* forced him to carry the execution post,
\v 22 and \add so\add* they \add all\add* arrived at Golgotha (which means ‘Place of the skull’).
\v 23 \add There\add* \add the soldiers\add* \add went to\add* give \add some\add* \add spiced\add* wine to \add Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add*, but he \add declined\add* \add it\add*.
\v 24 \add So\add* they \add carried out the execution\add*, taking \add Yeshua’s\add* clothes and \add drawing straws\add* \add to see who would get what\add*.\x + \xo 15:24: \xt Psa 22:18.\x*
\v 25 \add By now it was around 9am\add*, and they \add affixed\add* \add Yeshua\add* to the post.
\v 26 The charge had been written out and \add attached at the top\add*: “The king of the Yehudim \add (Jews)\add*.”
\v 27 \add That morning,\add* two thieves were \add also\add* executed there—one on \add each side\add* of \add Yeshua\add*.
\p
\v 28 ◘
\v 29 As \add people\add* passed by \add on that path\add*, they insulted \add Yeshua\add*, shaking their heads\x + \xo 15:29: \xt Psa 22:7; 109:25.\x* and shouting, “\add Hoy there\add*! You \add who reckoned\add* you could demolish the temple and rebuild it in three days,\x + \xo 15:29: \xt Yhn 2:19; Mrk 14:58.\x*
\v 30 come down from \add that\add* post \add and\add* save yourself.”
\p
\v 31 Similarly the chief priests and the \add religious teachers\add* \add laughed\add* together and mocked, “He \add did miracles for\add* others, but he can’t \add even\add* save himself.
\v 32 \add Now\add* if that \add so-called\add* ‘\nd chosen\nd* \add one\add*’ or ‘king of Yisrael’ \add (Israel)\add* would \add just\add* come down from \add there\add*, \em then\em* we’d \add be able\add* to believe \add him\add*.”
\p \add Even\add* the other \add two\add* being executed with him were deriding him.
\s1 Yeshua breathes his last
\r (Yhn 19:28-30; Mat. 27:45-56; Luke 23:44-49)
\p
\v 33 \add At noon\add*, it got \add dark\add* everywhere, until \add around\add* \add 3pm\add*,
\v 34 \add when\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* shouted loudly, “\wj My \+nd god\+nd*, my \+nd god\+nd*, why have you abandoned me?\wj*”\x + \xo 15:34: \xt Psa 22:1.\x*
\p
\v 35 Some of the \add people\add* standing nearby \add thought\add* he was calling \add the prophet\add* Eliyah \add (Elijah)\add*.
\v 36 One of them ran, and soaked a sponge in some sour wine, then put it on a stick and held it up for \add Yeshua\add* to drink,\x + \xo 15:36: \xt Psa 69:21.\x* saying, “\add Hang on\add*. Let’s see if Eliyah does come to get him down.”
\p
\v 37 But \add just then\add*, \nd Yeshua\nd* \add uttered\add* a loud cry and \add exhaled his last breath\add*.
\p
\v 38 (\add Back\add* in the temple, the curtain tore \add down the middle\add* from the top to the bottom.)\x + \xo 15:38: \xt Exo 26:31-33.\x*
\v 39 \add When\add* \add Yeshua\add* \add died\add*, the \add Romaios\add* \add commander\add* who had been standing \add back watching everything\add* said, “That man was \add definitely\add* \nd God’s\nd* son.”
\p
\v 40 \add Further back\add*, there was also \add a group of\add* women observing \add everything\add*. \add They\add* \add included\add* Miryam \add (Grk. Maria/Mariam)\add* from Magdala, Miryam the mother of \add young\add* Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add* and Yoseh, and Salome,\x + \xo 15:40-41: \xt Luk 8:2-3.\x*
\v 41 and others who had followed \add Yeshua\add* around Galil and \add helped look after\add* him, along with many others who had come \add down\add* to Yerushalem \add (Jerusalem)\add* with him.
\s1 Yosef boldly lays the body in a burial chamber
\r (Yhn 19:38-42; Mat. 27:57-61; Luke 23:50-56)
\p
\v 42 As evening came, it was \add now\add* the Preparation Day, i.e., the \add day before\add* the Rest Day.
\v 43 Yosef \add (Joseph)\add* (who’d come from Arimathaia \add city\add* and one who was waiting for the \add coming of\add* \nd God’s\nd* kingdom), a prominent council member, steeled himself up and went in to see \add the governor\add* to get \add permission\add* \add to transfer\add* \nd Yeshua’s\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* body.
\v 44 \add Governor\add* Pilatos \add (Pilate)\add* \add didn’t think he’d be dead yet\add*, so he called an \add army commander\add* to \add find out\add* if \add Yeshua\add* had indeed died.
\v 45 \add As soon as he found out\add*, he gave Yosef \add permission\add*,
\v 46 \add so\add* \add Yosef\add* \add and his companions\add* went and bought some linen \add burial\add* cloth and then, removing \add Yeshua’s body\add* from the post, wrapped it in the cloth and placed it in a \add burial chamber\add* that had been chiselled into a rockface. Then they rolled a rock \add across\add* the opening.
\v 47 \add Others\add* were watching \add and noted\add* where \add the body\add* had been laid, \add including\add* Miryam \add (Grk. Maria/Mariam)\add* from Magdala and Miryam who was Yoseh’ mother.
\c 16
\s1 The massive shock at the burial chamber
\r (Yhn 20:1-10; Mat. 28:1-8; Luke 24:1-12)
\p
\v 1 After the Rest Day was over, Miryam \add (Grk. Maria/Mariam)\add* from Magdala, Miryam the mother of Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add*, and Salome, \add all\add* went and bought \add some traditional burial\add* spices \add that evening\add* to take \add to the burial chamber and\add* \add place with\add* \add the body\add*.
\v 2 Then very early on \add Sunday\add* \add morning\add* they went to the chamber, arriving \add just as\add* the sun was rising.
\v 3 Then they \add realised that they\add* \add didn’t have anyone with them\add* \add to\add* roll the rock away \add that was covering the entrance\add*.
\v 4 \add However\add* when they looked, they saw that the very large rock had \add already\add* been rolled away,
\v 5 \add so\add* they went on into the \add burial chamber\add* and were totally stunned to find a young man dressed in white, sitting \add in there\add* \add at the side\add*.
\p
\v 6 He assured them, “Don’t be surprised. \add I know\add* you’re \add looking for\add* \nd Yeshua\nd* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* from Nazaret \add (Nazareth)\add*, the one who was executed on a post. \add But\add* see \add there\add* where his body was—he’s not there, because he \add came back to life\add*.
\v 7 \add So\add* \add you three\add* should go and tell his apprentices, and Kefa \add (Peter; Grk. Petros)\add* \add in particular\add*, that he’s going to go \add up\add* ahead of you all to Galil and you’ll see him \add up there\add*, \add just\add* as he already told you all.”\x + \xo 16:7: \xt Mat 26:32; Mrk 14:28.\x*
\p
\v 8 \add So\add* they left the chamber and \add took off running\add*, \add still\add* \add stunned\add* and shaking, and too scared \add to stop and\add* talk to anyone.
\rem It’s not certain whether or not the following longer ending of this document was actually penned by the same author (Markos/Mark), or whether it was appended slightly later. Expert scholars are divided on this, and hence it’s included here for your consideration:
\s1 \add The others don’t believe that Miryam saw Yeshua\add*
\r (Yhn 20:11-18; Mat. 28:9-10)
\p
\v 9 \add After coming back to life early on Sunday morning, Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add appeared first to Miryam\add* \add (Grk. Maria/Mariam)\add* \add from Magdala. (She was the one that he had once commanded seven demons to leave.)\add*
\v 10 \add After leaving him, she went and told his followers who were mourning and weeping at his loss.\add*
\v 11 \add But when she told them that he is alive again and that she’d seen him, they simply didn’t believe her.\add*
\s1 \add Yeshua appears to two of his followers\add*
\r (Luke 24:13-35)
\p
\v 12 \add Later on, Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add appeared in a different form to two of his followers on the path as they left Yerushalem\add* \add (Jerusalem)\add* \add and headed out to the countryside,\add*
\v 13 \add but when they hurried back and told the others, no one believed them.\add*
\s1 \add Yeshua appears to his apprentices and instructs them\add*
\r (Yhn 20:19-23; Mat. 28:16-20; Luke 24:36-49; Acts 1:6-8)
\p
\v 14 \add Later again when the eleven apprentices were sitting around eating, Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add appeared in the room and scolded them for not believing and for being so stubborn when they hadn’t believed others who had told them that he’d come back from the dead.\add*
\v 15 \add Then he instructed them, “\+wj Travel around all the world\+wj*\add* \add \+wj and tell everyone the good message.\+wj*\add*\x + \xo 16:15: \xt Acts 1:8.\x*
\v 16 \add \+wj Anyone who believes and gets immersed in water will be saved, however, those who refuse to believe will be condemned to death.\+wj*\add*
\v 17 \add \+wj Those who believe will be able to do miracles: they’ll be able to use my authority to command demons to leave and to speak new languages,\+wj*\add*
\v 18 \add \+wj and they’ll be able to pick up snakes. If they drink anything poisonous, it won’t hurt them, and they will place their hands on people and make them better.\+wj*”\add*
\s1 \add Yeshua is lifted up to heaven\add*
\r (Luke 24:50-53; Acts 1:9-11)
\p
\v 19 \add When Yeshua\add* \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \add had finished speaking, he was lifted up into heaven\x + \xo 16:19: \xt Acts 1:9-11.\x* and seated in the honoured place\add* \add next to God.\add*
\v 20 \add Then his followers went around preaching everywhere, and God worked through them and so they were able to confirm the truth of their preaching by doing miracles.\add*
